/* Promo scenes, promo twists, default promo lines and in-match moments: hand-written content, no engine logic.
   Loaded before the main script in index.html (it only holds plain data). Grep for a scene or key; don't read it whole. */
const SCENES={
callout:{
solo:{texts:['{A} storms to the ring, grabs a mic and waits for the crowd to settle.',
 {t:'{A} cuts off the commentary team, snatches a headset and climbs into the ring.',kk:'headset'},
 {al:'f',t:'{A} slaps hands all the way down the ramp before grabbing a mic. The building is electric.'},
 {al:'h',t:'{A} saunters out to a wall of boos and takes their sweet time picking up a mic.'}],ch:[
{t:'Cut a fiery speech about chasing the top prize',voice:'ambition',s:'mic',d:.1,p:3,ok:`"I came here for one reason: to be at the top of this card. And I'm not leaving until I get there." A good, loud reaction. {A} sounds like they mean it.`,g:`"Everybody in the back says they're ready for the top spot. Put the name that's on last across the ring from me and let them prove I'm wrong." The building comes up with {A}.`,no:`"Dreams. Hunger. Legacy." {A} hits every word in the book, and none of them land. The fans start drifting toward the concession stands.`,b:`"I want the... the gold. The top. The top gold. And I'm gonna get it, because — because I want it." A few fans clap to be polite.`},
{t:'Issue an open challenge to anyone in the back',s:'pop',d:.05,p:2,ok:`"Anybody back there wants a fight, I'm right here. Come on out." The crowd turns to the stage, buzzing about who might answer.`,g:`"No speech. No list. Anybody in the back who thinks they're better than me —" {A} points at the curtain and drops the mic to the mat. "Come and prove it." The arena buzzes, waiting.`,no:`"So, uh, if anybody in the back wants to step up, the door is open, my door's always open..." The challenge hangs in dead air.`,b:`"Anybody! I'll fight anybody. Anybody at all." A long wait. "...Except — no, anybody." Nobody comes out. The crowd starts to giggle.`},
{end:'g',t:'Keep it short: "I let my wrestling do the talking."',s:'ring',d:0,p:1,ok:`"I'm not much for talking. I let my wrestling do the talking." Simple and honest. A respectful cheer.`,g:`"You want a promo?" {A} looks at the mic, then at the crowd. "Watch my match." {A} hands the mic back and walks off. A real cheer.`,no:`"I'm, ah — I'm not a talker. You'll see me in the ring." It comes off as disinterested. The crowd gives it a polite nod.`,b:`"I let my wrestling do the talking." Silence. "...Which is why I'm talking right now." Someone in the front row laughs out loud.`},
{t:'Rattle off their record and call themselves unstoppable',s:'mic',d:.1,p:2,ok:`"Look at the record. Go ahead and circle every loss. You still have to put one there yourself." {A} sounds like a real threat.`,g:`"Watch the tape. Everybody who steps in there with me thinks they have one thing I can't answer. That's the part I look forward to." {A} sounds dangerous.`,no:`{A} unfolds a sheet. "January third, win. January tenth, win. January seventeenth—" By month four the crowd has stopped listening.`,b:`"I'm undefeated! Twelve and... and two. Twelve and — that's still pretty good." Somebody in the front row holds up their fingers to help.`},
{al:'f',t:'Thank the fans and promise never to let them down',s:'pop',d:.05,p:3,ok:`"This is YOUR house. And as long as I'm here, I will never let you down!" The fans are on their feet.`,g:`"I've had bad nights in this ring. Real bad. And every single time, you were louder the next week." {A} taps their chest. "So I'll never let you down. You never let me down." The fans are on their feet.`,no:`"I just wanna say thank you, from the bottom of my heart, truly, it means so much, every one of you..." It sounds like a greeting card. Polite applause.`,b:`"Thank you to all the fans. You're the best fans in the world. Thank you for the — for watching. On TV. And here." The applause is polite and a little confused.`},
{al:'f',t:'Dedicate their next match to the hometown crowd',s:'pop',d:.1,p:4,ok:`"My next match isn't for me. It's for this city. This one's for you!" A hometown chant breaks out across the arena.`,g:`{A} points to the upper deck. "I heard you up there before I could see you. When I get in that ring again, I want the person across from me to hear you too." A hometown chant shakes the place.`,no:`{A} raises the mic. "This one's for this city! And this state! And the whole region, really, and the country—" By "the whole country, really," the cheer has worn off.`,b:`"This match is for... this city!" {A} gets the city wrong. A beat of total silence, then a long, loud boo. Somebody in the production truck is getting fired.`},
{al:'f',t:'Call out the bullies in the locker room',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,ok:`"There's bullies in that locker room. And from now on, they've got to go through me." A huge cheer.`,g:`"There's people in that locker room who think the new kids are there to be stepped on. I know who you are. And I'm done watching." {A} looks right down the camera. The locker room just got a new sheriff.`,no:`"We all need to be kinder to each other. Backstage. And in life." It sounds like a school assembly. A few fans groan.`,b:`"To all the bullies in the back. You're... bullies. And that's — that's bad. Stop it." The crowd isn't sure if that was the whole speech. It was.`},
{al:'h',t:'Insult the local sports team',s:'mic',d:.05,p:2,ok:`"Your team stinks, your city stinks, and so do all of you." Cheap heat, and it works. Big boos.`,g:`"I drove past your stadium today. Looked a lot like your team. Empty, sad, and built for losing." The boos are thunderous. {A} soaks it up.`,no:`{A} sneers. "Your team couldn't win if the other team didn't show up!" It's a joke clearly written for a different city years ago. Even the heels in the back wince.`,b:`"Your team is the worst team! In the — the league they're in!" {A} names the wrong sport. The crowd laughs instead of booing.`},
{al:'h',t:'Refuse to speak until the crowd is completely silent',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,ok:`{A} waits, arms folded, while the boos rain down. "I'll wait. I've got all night." Five straight minutes of "you suck," and {A} soaks it up.`,g:`{A} stands perfectly still. Two minutes. Three. The "you suck" chant gets louder, and {A} just smiles. Then, softly: "Finished? Good. Now you can listen." The heat is unreal.`,no:`{A} folds their arms. "I'll wait." The standoff drags on. And on. Eventually the crowd stops booing because they're bored. "...Right. So." {A} starts talking to near silence.`,b:`{A} waits. "Okay, when you're — I'll start when —" Starts before it's quiet. Stops. Starts again. The crowd chants "Just say it!"`},
{al:'h',t:'Tell the fans they don\'t deserve a star like {A}',s:'mic',d:.1,p:2,ok:`"You people don't deserve me. You never did." The crowd boos loud and long. That's the job.`,g:`"I could be anywhere. Bigger cities. Better crowds. And I came here." A slow look around. "Honestly? I'm starting to think it was charity." The crowd is livid. {A} has never been more hated.`,no:`"You don't deserve a star like me, because I'm a star, and you're... not deserving." The fans shrug. Hard to hate someone this dull.`,b:`"You don't deserve me! I'm the best thing that's ever happened to you! Except for, like, family stuff." Laughter. Not the good kind.`},
{al:'h',t:'Shove the ring announcer for butchering their name',s:'ring',d:0,p:1,ok:`"It's {A}! Say it right!" {A} shoves the announcer into the ropes. The boos rattle the rafters.`,g:`{A} grabs the announcer by the lapels. "Say it right. Slowly. Like it matters. Because it does." The announcer whispers it perfectly, and {A} shoves them away anyway. Pure villainy.`,no:`{A} glares at the announcer. "It's not that hard. It's my name. Two syllables—" A weak little shove. The announcer barely moves.`,b:`{A} lunges at the announcer. "Say it RIGHT!" {A} misses and stumbles into the ropes. The announcer reads the name again, correctly, to cheers.`}]},
duo:{texts:['{A} marches out and demands that {B} come face them right now.',
 {t:'{A} interrupts {B}\'s entrance and blocks the ramp.',kk:'here ramp'},
 {al:'f',vs:'h',t:'{A} has had enough of {B}\'s cheap shots and calls {B} out to a massive ovation.'},
 {al:'h',vs:'f',t:'{A} strolls out, smirking, and calls the fans\' hero {B} a fraud.'},
 {al:'h',vs:'h',t:'{A} calls out {B} — two villains who can\'t stand each other. The crowd doesn\'t know who to boo.'},
 {al:'f',vs:'f',t:'{A} calls out {B}. Two fan favorites, one question: who\'s the best?'}],ch:[
{t:'Get personal and go after {B}',s:'mic',d:.2,h:14,p:2,ok:`"Everybody thinks you're so great, {B}. I know the truth. You're scared, and you know I'm better than you." The crowd gasps. {B} has to answer.`,g:`"I'll give you this, {B}. You don't quit. Not when they said you were too small, not when your body gave out." A pause. "So I'll have to take it from you." Dead silence, then the boos. {B} has to answer that.`,no:`{A} digs for something personal. "Remember Dayton, {B}? Six years ago? The thing with the van?" Nobody remembers Dayton. The room drifts away.`,b:`"{B}! Your family... your family is — they probably don't even —" A long pause. "You know what you did." Nobody knows what {B} did. A "What?" chant starts.`},
{key:1,t:'Lay down a challenge for a match',voice:'challenge',ch:1,s:'mic',d:.05,h:9,p:2,ok:`"{B}, it's simple. You and me. One on one. Say yes." {B} hears it loud and clear. This one is on.`,g:`"I want you in that ring, {B}. One match. Say yes or let everyone see you walk away." {A} holds the stare. {B} hears it loud and clear.`,no:`{A} pulls out a list. "One fall, no count-outs, no outside help, a ref we both agree on, a two-week notice period—" By the third clause the fans aren't sure what was just said.`,b:`"{B}! I challenge you to a — to a fight. A match. A match fight. At {PPV}. Or before. Whenever." The fans aren't sure what was just agreed to.`},
{nhk:'here',gone:'no',t:'Wait for {B} and stare them down in silence',s:'pop',d:.1,h:11,p:2,ok:`{A} lowers the mic. "Come out here, {B}." {B} comes out, and they stand nose to nose in silence. The crowd is on its feet.`,g:`{A} drops the mic and waits. When {B} finally walks out, {A} says only one word, off-mic: "Closer." The whole building is on its feet, and the first person to blink loses.`,no:`{A} waits. "I'll stand here all night, {B}." And waits. {B} never comes out, and {A} is left standing alone.`,b:`{A} stares at the stage. "I'm waiting, {B}. I'm — still waiting." {B} walks out behind them, through the crowd. The fans laugh. {A} spins around way too late.`},
{nhk:'here',gone:'no',end:'ok g',ri:'brawl',t:'Call {B} down for a fight right here, right now',s:'ring',d:.15,h:15,p:1,ok:`"Forget the next show. You and me, right here, right now!" {B} charges the ring and it's a brawl!`,g:`"No more talking. Get down here." {A} throws the mic away and points. {B} charges the ring, and it's a brawl before the first word is finished.`,no:`"Come on down, {B}, let's do this, right now, I mean it, I'm serious..." {B} walks off and leaves {A} fuming alone.`,b:`"Get down here right now!" {B} shows up immediately. {A} visibly wasn't ready and backs into the corner. The crowd laughs.`},
 {hk:'celebration',ri:'insult',t:"Grab {B}'s celebration confetti and dump it on their head",s:'pop',d:.05,h:10,p:2,ok:`{A} dumps the confetti right on {B}'s head. "Party's over." The crowd roars.`,g:`{A} empties the confetti over {B}'s head and leans in close. "Enjoy the party. It's the last one you'll have this year." The party's over. The crowd roars.`,no:`{A} tips the confetti over {B}. "Party's ov—" Most of it blows back into {A}'s own face. A sad little puff.`,b:`{A} yanks at the confetti cannon. "Party's over! It's — why won't it —" It fires into the crowd. The front row cheers. {B} applauds.`},
 {ri:'shove',hk:'here',nff:1,t:"Shove {B} back the way they came",s:'ring',d:.1,h:12,p:2,ok:`{A} meets {B} at the bottom of the ramp and shoves them back. "Not tonight." {B} stumbles back up the ramp.`,g:`{A} shoves {B} back up the ramp, one step at a time. "Back. Back. This ring isn't yours yet." {B} stumbles to the stage. Message delivered.`,no:`{A} shoves {B}. "Back up the ramp. Now." {B} doesn't budge an inch. {A} pushes again. It looks more like a negotiation than a threat.`,b:`{A} shoves {B}. "Get — get out of my —" {A} bounces off them and nearly falls over. {B} doesn't move. Somebody yells "Timber!"`},
 {hk:'screen',t:"Turn to the big screen and talk straight to {B}",s:'mic',d:.1,h:10,p:3,ok:`"{B}! I know you're watching. Every time you see my face, I want you to know I'm coming for you." Face to face, even through a screen. {B} looks rattled.`,g:`{A} turns to the screen, close enough to fog it. "You're watching from the back, {B}? Good. Get used to watching. That's all you'll be doing at {PPV}." {B} looks rattled.`,no:`{A} squares up to the screen. "{B}, I know you can hear me, and I've got a lot to say, so get comfortable—" The feed cuts out mid-sentence, and nobody's sure how much {B} heard.`,b:`{A} jabs a finger at the big screen. "{B}! I see you! I'm coming for—" It's the wrong screen. The camera finds {B} on the other one, waving.`},
{al:'f',vs:'h',t:'Promise the fans {B} will finally get what\'s coming',s:'pop',d:.05,h:10,p:3,ok:`"You've all waited a long time for this. At {PPV}, {B} is finally getting what's coming to them!" The crowd roars.`,g:`"For two years, {B} has done whatever they want and walked away smiling." {A} turns to the crowd. "You've waited a long time for somebody to make {B} stop. You're done waiting." The crowd roars.`,no:`"And at the end of the day, {B} will get theirs, because, you know, what goes around comes around." {B} laughs from the stage and the moment fizzles.`,b:`"{B} is gonna get what's coming! What's coming is me! And... justice. Me and justice." {B} laughs from the stage. The fans laugh too.`},
{al:'f',vs:'h',t:'Call {B} a coward who hides behind cheap tricks',s:'mic',d:.1,h:12,p:2,ok:`"{B}, you're a coward. You hide behind cheap tricks because you can't beat me straight up!" The "Coward!" chants ring out and {B} has nowhere to hide.`,g:`"You call it strategy. A chair when the ref's down. A friend in the crowd. A run up the ramp." {A} shakes their head. "We call it what it is, {B}. Coward." The chant starts on its own.`,no:`{A} calls {B} a coward, then calls them a coward again, slightly louder. {B} flips it around: "Smart, not cowardly." The crowd laughs.`,b:`"You're a coward, {B}! A big coward! Because you — you do coward things!" {B} flips it right back. The crowd laughs at {A}.`},
{nhk:'screen',al:'f',vs:'f',gone:'b',t:'Offer {B} a handshake — may the best competitor win',s:'pop',d:.05,h:7,p:3,ok:`"No tricks. No excuses. May the best one win." They shake hands. Respect on both sides, and suddenly everyone needs to see this match.`,g:`{A} holds out a hand. "Best I've ever stood across from. That's why I'm going to enjoy beating you." {B} shakes it. Suddenly everyone needs to see this match.`,no:`{A} holds out a hand. "I respect you. I respect what you've done, the people you've beaten, the nights you've had, and I think it's important that we—" {B} leaves the hand hanging, and the speech gets more awkward with every word.`,b:`{A} reaches out. "Hey, uh, may the — the better one — good luck." It turns into a fist bump. Then a hug. Then a handshake again. {B} walks off. Awkward.`},
{al:'f',vs:'h',t:'Tell {B} this one is for everyone they\'ve ever hurt',s:'mic',d:.15,h:13,p:3,ok:`"This one isn't for me, {B}. It's for everybody you ever hurt. They're all coming with me!" Goosebumps. The crowd rises with {A}.`,g:`"This isn't about me." {A} reads off names, one by one — everyone {B} has hurt, everyone they walked past. "At {PPV}, they're all in my corner." Goosebumps. The crowd rises with {A}.`,no:`"This is for everybody, and I mean everybody, who ever got hurt, by anybody..." It comes off melodramatic and the crowd giggles.`,b:`"This is for everyone you ever hurt! Which is a lot. Like, at least six people." The crowd giggles at the wrong moment.`},
{al:'h',t:'Mock {B}\'s catchphrase in a ridiculous voice',s:'mic',d:.1,h:13,p:2,ok:`{A} puts on a squeaky voice and does {B}'s catchphrase. "That's you. That's what you sound like." The fans are outraged, and {B} looks ready to explode.`,g:`{A} does {B}'s catchphrase in a perfect, whiny voice — then drops it cold. "Every week the same line. Every week the same result. Second place." The fans are outraged. {B} looks ready to explode.`,no:`{A} pinches their nose and does {B}'s catchphrase. Then does it again. "And another one — wait, here's the good bit." The impression goes on too long. The crowd sides with {B} even harder.`,b:`{A} attempts {B}'s catchphrase. "It's... the one with the... you know the one." The whole crowd corrects {A} at once, then chants it louder than ever.`},
{al:'h',t:'Play {B}\'s most embarrassing loss on the big screen',s:'mic',d:.15,h:16,p:2,ok:`"Let's all watch {B}'s greatest moment!" The loss plays on the big screen, and {B} has to watch it in front of everyone. Brutal.`,g:`The loss plays on the big screen. {A} doesn't say a word until it ends. Then: "Watch it again, {B}. That's what everybody here thinks about when they see you." Brutal.`,no:`The video won't load. {A} stands there waiting. And waiting. "Is it — can we — okay."`,b:`{A} points at the screen. "Everybody watch {B} lose!" The wrong video plays: {B}'s greatest win. The crowd goes wild. {A} stares at the screen in horror.`},
{al:'h',vs:'f',t:'Blame {B}\'s fans for every loss',s:'mic',d:.1,h:12,p:2,ok:`"You know why {B} keeps losing? Because of you people. You made {B} soft!" The whole building turns on {A}.`,g:`"Every time {B} loses, I hear the same excuse from you people. '{B} tried so hard.' No. You let {B} settle for trying. You never once asked for better." The whole building turns on {A}. Mission accomplished.`,no:`{A} starts a theory. "Statistically, {B} loses more in towns with louder crowds, which means — follow me here — that you, the fans, are the problem, and also the weather—" Four minutes in, nobody is following.`,b:`"{B} loses because of the fans! Because you cheer too much. Or not enough. One of them." Nobody follows it, including {A}.`},
{al:'h',vs:'f',t:'Pay a fan in the front row to boo {B}',s:'luck',d:0,h:9,p:1,ok:`{A} hands a fan in the front row a twenty. "Let them have it." The fan boos {B} with gusto. The rest of the crowd boos {A}. Perfect.`,g:`{A} slips a fan a twenty and points. The fan boos {B} with gusto. "See? Even your own people have a price, {B}." The rest of the crowd boos {A}. Perfect.`,no:`{A} hands the fan a twenty. "Boo them. Loud." The fan pockets the money and cheers for {B} anyway.`,b:`{A} hands the fan a twenty. "Okay, now — boo. Boo them." The fan starts a "{B}!" chant. "Can I have that back?" {A} asks for the money back on camera.`},
{al:'h',vs:'h',gone:'no',t:'Offer {B} an alliance… then laugh in their face',s:'mic',d:.2,h:15,p:2,ok:`"{B}, think about it. You and me, together?" {B} actually considers it, and then {A} laughs in {B}'s face. Now {B} looks like a fool.`,g:`"You and me, {B}? We'd run this place." {A} lets it hang, long enough that {B} almost nods. Then the laugh. "I'd never team with someone I'm about to replace." {B} looks like a fool.`,no:`{A} spreads their arms. "{B}, partners. Think about it. Tag titles, a nice logo, matching jackets, a theme song—" {B} sees the punchline coming a mile away and walks off laughing.`,b:`{A} offers the alliance, then forgets to laugh. {B} accepts. {A} panics. "No, I was kidding!" The moment dies.`}]}},
attack:{
duo:{texts:[{kk:'back interview',nff:1,t:'{B} is mid-interview backstage when {A} creeps up from behind.'},
 {kk:'ramp entrance',nff:1,t:'{B} is making their entrance when the lights go out. When they come back, {A} is right behind them.'},
 {kk:'ring',al:'f',vs:'h',t:'After weeks of {B}\'s dirty tricks, {A} finally snaps and charges down the aisle.'},
 {kk:'ring autographs',al:'h',t:'{B} is signing autographs at ringside when {A} hops the barricade.'}],ch:[
{nff:1,end:'ok',t:'A brutal assault with a steel chair',s:'ring',d:.15,h:20,p:1,ok:`A brutal chair shot. {A} drops the chair on {B}. "Stay down." {A} walks off as medics rush in.`,g:`{A} swings the chair, once, flush. Then crouches over {B} and says, quietly enough that only the camera hears: "That's for {PPV}. In advance." Medics rush in.`,no:`{A} swings the chair. "This is for—" {B} ducks and fights {A} off.`,b:`{A} winds up. "Here comes the — hey!" So slowly that {B} turns, catches the chair and rips it away.`},
{hk:'ring|ramp',nff:1,end:'ok g',t:'Hit and run through the crowd',s:'luck',d:0,h:12,p:1,ok:`{A} comes over the barricade, one shot, and is gone. "Bye, {B}!" In and out before security can react.`,g:`In and out before security can react. On the way through the crowd {A} turns back and yells: "Same time next week!" The fans in that section can't believe it.`,no:`{A} lands the shot. "See ya—" Security blocks the exit, and {A} has to run the long way around.`,b:`{A} lands the shot and runs. "Later, lose— whoa!" A cable. {A} gets up and runs the wrong way. Awkward.`},
{nff:1,t:'Attack, then grab the mic and gloat',s:'mic',d:.2,h:18,p:3,ok:`{A} grabs a mic and stands over {B}. "That's what happens when you mess with me!" Huge heat.`,g:`{A} stands over {B}, breathing hard, and crouches down with the mic. "Look at me. Look at me. This is what the next three weeks are gonna feel like." Chilling.`,no:`{A} grabs a mic over {B}. "This is what happens. This is what always happens. Let me explain exactly what happens—" {B} is up before {A} finishes.`,b:`"And THAT is why — that's what you — you see what you get?" {A} trails off. {B} is already getting up.`},
{nff:1,t:'Hit the finisher on the concrete floor',s:'ring',d:.2,h:21,p:2,ok:`{A} hits the finisher on the concrete. "Get a doctor." The sound echoes down the hall. {B} isn't moving.`,g:`The finisher on the concrete. {A} stands, looks straight into the camera and puts a finger to their lips. "Shh. They're resting." {B} isn't moving.`,no:`{A} hoists {B}. "Concrete doesn't give—" {B} slips free and {A} crashes hard into the wall.`,b:`{A} lifts {B}. "On the floor! On the — whoa—" Both of them crash into the wall together. {B} gets up first.`},
{al:'f',vs:'h',gone:'no b',t:'Give {B} a taste of their own medicine',s:'ring',d:.1,h:16,p:3,ok:`{A} grabs {B}'s favorite weapon. "Remember this? Your turn." Payback! The fans have waited weeks for this.`,g:`{A} grabs the same chair {B} used three weeks ago. "Remember this?" One shot. Payback, and the fans have waited weeks for it.`,no:`{A} goes after {B}. "Payback time!" {B} slips away before {A} can land a shot.`,b:`{A} copies {B}'s trick. "Rake, then — kick? Then the — what came next?" {B} slips away, laughing.`},
{nhk:'lot',al:'f',vs:'h',gone:'ok g',t:'Chase {B} out of the building',s:'pop',d:.05,h:12,p:2,ok:`{A} chases {B} into the parking lot. "Run! Keep running!" The fans go wild.`,g:`{B} bolts for the parking lot with {A} right behind. {A} yells after them: "You can run to your car, {B}! I know where you park!" The fans go wild.`,no:`{A} sprints after {B}. "Get back here!" {B} ducks into a car and speeds off. {A} kicks the dust.`,b:`{A} chases {B}. "You can't — wait, which way —" {A} takes the wrong exit. {B} drives past, honking.`},
{al:'f',up:1,t:'Stop short and let the refs pull them apart',s:'mic',d:.1,h:8,p:3,ok:`{A} lets the refs pull them apart. "Next time, nobody's stopping me." {A} keeps the moral high ground.`,g:`The refs pull them apart. {A} doesn't fight it, just points at {B}. "That's the last time anybody stops me." {A} keeps the high ground, and the promise lands.`,no:`{A} stops short. "Okay. Okay." The refs step in, and it looks like {A} lost their nerve.`,b:`{A} stops. "Fine." Then lunges. "No — not fine!" The refs stop them anyway. It looks like {A} doesn't know what they want.`},
{al:'h',t:'Stomp away at {B}\'s knee until they can\'t stand',s:'ring',d:.1,h:20,p:1,ok:`{A} stomps away at {B}'s knee. "Walk on that." {B} can't stand. Vicious and calculated. {B} is helped to the back.`,g:`Stomp after stomp on the knee, until {B} can't stand. {A} kneels down: "Walk to {PPV}. I dare you." Vicious and calculated. {B} is helped to the back.`,no:`{A} goes for the knee. "Let's see you walk—" {B} kicks {A} away and limps to safety.`,b:`{A} stomps. "That's for — wait, wrong knee." Switches. Gets kicked off. {B} limps to safety.`},
{al:'h',gone:'b',t:'Spray-paint their name on {B}\'s back',s:'luck',d:.05,h:14,p:2,ok:`{A} shakes a spray can. "Hold still. Art takes time." Their own name, across {B}'s back. A humiliating image for every highlight reel.`,g:`{A} sprays their name across {B}'s back in big red letters, then signs the bottom like a painting. "Masterpiece." A humiliating image for every highlight reel.`,no:`{A} shakes the can. "Let me sign my work—" It's nearly empty. The name comes out faint and patchy, barely readable.`,b:`{A} shakes the can. "Hold still — why isn't it — come ON." Empty. {A} tries to write it with the cap. {B} gets up and leaves.`},
{hk:'ring|ramp',al:'h',t:'Drag {B} up the stage and hit the finisher off it',s:'ring',d:.2,h:22,p:2,ok:`{A} drags {B} up to the stage. "Everybody watching? Good." Then the finisher off it. An iconic, sickening visual.`,g:`{A} drags {B} up to the stage and stops at the edge. "Everybody look." Then the finisher off the stage. An iconic, sickening visual. The crowd is stunned into silence.`,no:`{A} drags {B} up the stage. "Watch this—" Security swarms the stage before {A} can finish the job.`,b:`{A} drags {B} up the stage. "Come — on — you're heavy—" Security arrives while {A} is still looking for a grip.`},
{al:'h',t:'Bring a masked accomplice for a two-on-one',s:'luck',d:.1,h:17,p:1,ok:`A masked accomplice joins in. Two on one. {A} grins at the camera. "Guess who." {B} is down and out.`,g:`A masked figure, two on one, and {B} is down. The partner leaves without a word. {A} grins: "Not telling." Who was that? Nobody knows.`,no:`A masked figure joins the attack. {A} yells, "Go, go, go!" The mask slips in the chaos, and the camera gets a clear look.`,b:`The accomplice's mask comes off in the chaos. {A} panics. "Run, Darren! RUN!" Oops.`}]}},
interview:{
solo:{texts:['{A} sits down for a one-on-one interview under a single spotlight.',
 {kk:'fans',al:'f',t:'Surrounded by fan signs, {A} sits down for a heartfelt interview.'},
 {kk:'late',al:'h',t:'{A} shows up an hour late to the interview, sunglasses on indoors.'}],ch:[
{t:'Open up about their journey',s:'mic',d:.15,p:4,ok:`"It wasn't easy getting here. A lot of people told me no. I'm still here." Honest and straightforward. The fans connect with {A}.`,g:`"I slept in my car for a year. I'm not proud of it. I'm not ashamed of it either." {A} takes a moment. "Every one of those nights got me to this chair." Genuine and moving. A new connection.`,no:`{A} leans back. "It wasn't easy getting here. A lot of people told me no." The exact words they used last time. It feels rehearsed, and viewers tune out.`,b:`"It's been a journey. A long journey. A journey of... it's been long." The interviewer waits for more. There isn't more.`},
{t:'Stay cocky and confident',s:'mic',d:.05,p:2,ok:`"Nobody on this roster can hang with me. I know it. They know it." {A} sounds like a star.`,g:`{A} leans back. "You want to know my weakness? I'm honestly asking. I've been looking for years." Smug, funny and dangerous. {A} oozes star power.`,no:`"I'm the best. I'm the greatest. I'm the most talented. I'm the..." The confidence tips into a list, and the list never ends.`,b:`"I'm the best, I'm the — sorry, can I start that again?" The interviewer nods. The second take isn't better.`},
{t:'Break down their game plan like a pro athlete',s:'ring',d:.05,p:2,ok:`"I've studied the tape. I know what's coming, and I know how to beat it." Smart and credible. {A} looks like a real threat.`,g:`"First four minutes, I take the legs. Then the hands, so you can't grab the ropes. Then I wait." {A} sips their water. "I'm not hoping to win. I'm planning to." Smart and credible.`,no:`{A} leans forward. "On the third rope break, they always shift left. On the fifth, right. Except on Thursdays, when—" Too much detail. The interviewer has to cut them off.`,b:`"My game plan is to... win. Through winning. With wrestling." The interviewer asks a follow-up question. {A} repeats the answer.`},
{t:'Tease a secret they aren\'t ready to share yet',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,ok:`"I've got something planned. You'll see it soon. That's all I'll say." Everybody watching is theorizing.`,g:`The interviewer asks the question again. {A} smiles and says nothing for a long, long time. "Ask me after {PPV}." Every fan watching is theorizing.`,no:`"There's things happening, maybe, things that I can't talk about, but there are things." It comes off as vague rather than mysterious.`,b:`"I can't tell you the secret." The interviewer nods. "It's about —" {A} catches themselves, too late. Half the secret is out.`},
{al:'f',t:'Thank the fans who carried them through the hard times',s:'pop',d:.1,p:4,ok:`"When things were hard, you were there. I'll never forget that. Thank you." Simple and heartfelt. The fans love it.`,g:`"When I got hurt, I got letters. Hundreds. One kid sent me a drawing every single week." {A} stops, swallows hard. "I still have every one." Not a dry eye anywhere.`,no:`{A} takes a breath. "Thank you to everyone. To Mike, who drove me. To the hotel shuttle guy, Ray—" Sincere, but the moment passes.`,b:`"Thank you for always being there. Thank you. Thanks." {A} clearly had more and lost it. The interviewer says "Thank you" back.`},
{hk:'fans',al:'f',t:'Surprise a young fan with their signed gear',s:'pop',d:.05,p:3,ok:`{A} hands a young fan their signed gear. "This is yours now." A big hug. The kid's reaction is going viral by the end of the night.`,g:`{A} hands over the gear and crouches down to eye level. "You keep this safe for me. I'm going to need it back when you're the champion." The kid's reaction is going viral by the end of the night.`,no:`{A} hands over the gear. "This is for you, buddy!" The kid is too starstruck to react. Sweet, but quiet.`,b:`{A} signs the gear. "To my biggest fan, from — The Masked Vortex. No, wait." The wrong name, a habit from an old gimmick. The kid politely says thank you.`},
 {hk:'family',al:'f',t:"Let their kid ask the last question",s:'pop',d:.05,p:4,ok:`"Are you going to win?" {A} smiles: "Yeah, buddy. I'm gonna win." The biggest reaction of the night.`,g:`"Are you going to win?" {A} kneels down to their kid. "I promised you I would. And when have I ever broken a promise?" The kid shakes their head. The biggest reaction of the night.`,no:`{A} smiles at their kid. "Go ahead, ask me anything." The kid asks if they can go home now. {A} laughs, but the moment's gone.`,b:`{A} hands their kid the mic. "Last question, buddy." The kid asks why {A} lost last month. {A} doesn't have an answer. The kid shrugs and walks off.`},
 {hk:'home',t:"Point out the worn-out ring where they learned to take a bump",s:'mic',d:.05,p:4,ok:`"This is where I learned. Every bump, every mistake. This ring made me." A quiet, real moment. The fans see where it all started.`,g:`{A} runs a hand along the ropes. "Broke my nose on this turnbuckle. Cried in that corner." A small laugh. "Best years of my life." A quiet, real moment.`,no:`{A} runs a hand along the ropes. "This is where I learned it all." The ring has been replaced. "Well. The old one was here." It's not the same.`,b:`"This is the ring where I —" {A} looks closer. "No. This isn't it. They changed it." The camera crew quietly packs up.`},
 {hk:'gym',t:"Answer every question between sets on the bench press",s:'ring',d:.1,p:3,ok:`Rep. "Scared?" Rep. "No." {A} answers every question between sets. Short answers, heavy weight. Intense and believable.`,g:`Rep. "Am I scared?" Rep. "I've been scared since I was nine." Rep. "Doesn't stop me lifting." The bar goes back on the rack. Intense and believable.`,no:`Rep. "Ready?" Rep. "Yeah." Rep. "Hnngh." The answers get shorter, and the last few are just grunts.`,b:`{A} pushes the bar up. "I'm ready to — hhh — to — hhh —" {A} runs out of breath and has to rack it. The spotter finishes the sentence with a helpful "win."`},
 {hk:'late',al:'h',t:"Blame the interviewer for 'starting early'",s:'mic',d:.05,p:3,ok:`"You started early. That's on you, not me." An hour late and somehow it's everyone else's fault. Infuriating.`,g:`"You started without me? That's an hour I'll never get back, and frankly I'm offended you thought you could." {A} takes off the sunglasses. "Start over. From the top." Infuriating.`,no:`{A} glares at the interviewer. "You started early." The interviewer just points at the clock. {A} has no comeback.`,b:`"You started early!" The interviewer points at the clock. "...My clock was different." Nobody buys it.`},
{al:'h',end:'ok g no',t:'Walk out halfway through a question',s:'luck',d:.05,p:2,ok:`Halfway through the question, {A} stands. "I'm done here." And walks out. The interviewer is left stammering.`,g:`Halfway through the question, {A} stands up. "That's a three-week-old question. I'm a today person." And walks. The interviewer is left stammering.`,no:`Halfway through the question, {A} stands. "We're done." And walks out. Nobody notices until the camera cuts back.`,b:`{A} stands. "I'm out of here!" Storms out through the wrong door, into a broom closet, and has to walk back past the camera. "...Different door."`},
{al:'h',t:'Bully the interviewer until they apologize',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,ok:`{A} leans in. "Say sorry." Leans closer. "Say it." The interviewer apologizes. Uncomfortable and mean, which is exactly the point.`,g:`"Say it again. Slower. Now apologize." The interviewer does, voice shaking. {A} pats their cheek. "See? That's how we build trust." Uncomfortable, mean and absolutely magnetic.`,no:`{A} leans in. "Apologize. Now." The interviewer doesn't blink and says "For what? Asking a question you couldn't answer?" The interviewer wins the exchange.`,b:`{A} tries to intimidate the interviewer, who isn't intimidated in the slightest. "Are we done?" "...Yes."`},
{al:'h',t:'Read a list of everyone who has disappointed them',s:'mic',d:.1,p:2,ok:`{A} pulls out a list. "My old trainer. The booker who said no. And every fan who ever doubted me." Petty and hilarious. Fans at home are fuming.`,g:`{A} unfolds a long sheet of paper. "My parents. My first trainer. This interviewer, as of four minutes ago." A pause. "And you. Every single one of you watching." Petty, specific and hilarious. Fans at home are furious.`,no:`{A} reads on. "Number thirty-nine, my dentist. Number forty, my dentist's receptionist—" By name forty, even {A} looks bored.`,b:`{A} reads the list, then realizes it's their grocery list. They keep going anyway. "Eggs. Eggs have disappointed me."`}]},
duo:{texts:['{A} and {B} sit across from each other for a tense interview.',
 {al:'f',vs:'h',t:'The interviewer barely gets a word in as {B} sneers across the table at {A}.'},
 {al:'h',vs:'h',t:'Two villains, one table, zero manners. {A} and {B} sit down.'},
 {al:'f',vs:'f',t:'{A} and {B} sit down with nothing but respect — for now.'}],ch:[
{t:'Calmly dissect {B}\'s weaknesses',s:'mic',d:.15,h:10,p:3,ok:`"I've watched your matches, {B}. You slow down late. You get sloppy. And I'll be waiting." {B} is visibly rattled.`,g:`"Your left shoulder's been taped for a month. You don't throw the big kick after ten minutes anymore. You look at the clock." {A} folds their hands. "I don't need to beat you, {B}. I just need to wait." Surgical. {B} is visibly rattled.`,no:`{A} reads from a notebook. "Weakness one: cardio. Weakness two: the left knee. Weakness three—" {B} laughs it off. "You've been watching tape of somebody else." {B} wins the exchange.`,b:`"Your weakness is... you're weak. In the — your weak parts." {B} laughs. The interviewer looks at the floor.`},
{nff:1,end:'ok g no',t:'Flip the table',s:'ring',d:.05,h:16,p:1,ok:`{A} stands. "We're done talking." {A} flips the table into {B}, and the segment ends in a pull-apart brawl. Chaos!`,g:`{A} stands, flips the table, and before it lands says: "Interview's over." Chaos! The segment ends in a pull-apart brawl.`,no:`{A} grabs the edge of the table. "Interview's over!" It's bolted down on one side and barely moves. They brawl anyway, half-heartedly.`,b:`{A} grabs the table. "Interview's — hang on." It barely moves. {A} tries again. And again. {B} helps them flip it, out of pity.`},
{al:'h',t:'Offer a handshake… then pull it away',s:'mic',d:.1,h:13,p:2,ok:`{A} holds out a hand. "Good luck, {B}." Then pulls it away at the last second. "Kidding." Pure mind games.`,g:`{A} offers the hand, warm, sincere. {B} reaches for it. {A} slides it back to fix their hair. "Oh — did you think...? That's adorable." Pure mind games.`,no:`{A} offers the hand. "Let's keep it classy—" {A} pulls it away, but {B} saw it coming and slaps it aside. "Classy. Sure." {B} gets the last word.`,b:`{A} snatches the hand back before {B} even moves. "Ha! Too slow!" {B} never reached for it. Nobody quite understands what happened.`},
{end:'ok g no',t:'Walk out and leave {B} talking to an empty chair',s:'luck',d:.05,h:9,p:2,ok:`{A} stands up mid-answer. "I've heard enough." {A} walks out while {B} is still talking, leaving {B} fuming at an empty chair. The fans howl.`,g:`{A} stands mid-sentence and buttons their jacket. "Keep going. I'm sure it's riveting." And leaves. {B} keeps talking for a good ten seconds before they notice. The fans howl.`,no:`{A} stands. "I don't have to listen to this." {A} walks out, and {B} just keeps talking to the camera. {B} wins the segment.`,b:`{A} stands. "I'm out. Bye." {A} walks out, then comes back. "Forgot my water." {B} hands it to them.`},
{al:'f',t:'Stay calm while {B} rants, then deliver one perfect line',s:'mic',d:.15,h:12,p:3,ok:`{A} lets {B} yell it out, then says: "You done? Good. See you at {PPV}." {B} has nothing. Perfect.`,g:`{B} rants for a full minute. {A} lets it finish, then waits three more seconds. "I'll see you at {PPV}, {B}. Bring all of that with you." The studio goes silent. Perfect.`,no:`{A} waits for the perfect moment. "When you're — when you're done—" {B} never stops yelling. The line gets lost in the noise.`,b:`{A} jumps in a beat too early. "See you at {PPV}!" It lands over {B}'s yelling. Nobody hears it.`},
{al:'f',vs:'h',t:'Play footage of {B}\'s cheating on the studio monitor',s:'pop',d:.05,h:11,p:2,ok:`"Let's roll the tape." The footage of {B} cheating plays on the monitor. Caught red-handed. {B} has no answer.`,g:`The footage plays: a hand on the ropes, feet on the ropes, the ref looking away, all of it {B}. {A} doesn't speak until it ends. "Tell them it's doctored, {B}. I'll wait." Caught red-handed.`,no:`{A} points at the monitor. "Watch closely." The footage is grainy and hard to follow. {B} shrugs. "That's doctored." Some fans buy it.`,b:`{A} points at the monitor. "And here's {B}, cheating!" The wrong footage plays: {A} pulling the tights in a match last year. The interviewer coughs.`},
{al:'f',vs:'f',t:'Admit {B} is the toughest opponent they\'ve ever faced',s:'mic',d:.05,h:6,p:3,ok:`"I'll be honest, {B}. You're the toughest opponent I've ever had. And I still think I win." Class. Now everyone wants to see these two go at it.`,g:`"You're the toughest I've ever faced, {B}. I've lost sleep over you. I mean that." A beat. "Which is exactly why I'm going to beat you. I've had a lot of time to think." Class. Everyone wants to see this.`,no:`{A} keeps going. "Toughest I've faced. Best I've seen. Honestly, if I lose, there's no shame in it at all—" It starts to sound like {A} is already making excuses for losing.`,b:`"You're the toughest opponent I've ever faced. Like, really tough. I might lose." The interviewer slowly turns to the camera.`},
{al:'h',t:'Talk over {B} every time they speak',s:'mic',d:.05,h:10,p:1,ok:`{B} starts to answer. {A} cuts in. "Nope." {B} tries again. {A} again: "Still no." {A} talks over {B} every single time. {B} looks ready to snap.`,g:`Every time {B} opens their mouth, {A} finishes the sentence for them, calmly, wrong. "What {B} means is, they're scared." Never louder than needed. {B} looks ready to snap.`,no:`{A} talks over {B}. "No. No. Let me finish. And another thing — and — well." {A} runs out of things to say. {B} simply waits, then gets the last word.`,b:`{A} talks over {B}. "No, listen, the thing is — the thing — what was I saying?" {B} picks up exactly where they left off.`},
{al:'h',vs:'f',t:'Insult {B}\'s hometown to their face',s:'mic',d:.1,h:14,p:2,ok:`"Your hometown is a dump, {B}. No wonder you turned out like this." Low blow. {B} is ready to flip the table.`,g:`"I went to your hometown, {B}. Lovely place. I see why you left. I see why nobody else ever does." Low blow. {B} is ready to flip the table.`,no:`{A} sneers. "Your hometown? Cleveland? Dump." {B} smiles. "I'm from Tulsa." The moment's gone.`,b:`{A} insults {B}'s hometown, then admits they've never been there. "I heard it's bad though." The interviewer laughs at {A}.`}]}},
contract:{
duo:{texts:['A table, two chairs and a contract for {A} vs {B}. Both sit down.',
 {kk:'lawyer security',al:'h',t:'{A} arrives at the contract signing with a lawyer and two security guards.'},
 {al:'f',vs:'h',t:'{A} sits across from {B}, ready for anything — they know {B} won\'t play fair.'}],ch:[
{nff:1,t:'Sign it — then put {B} through the table',s:'ring',d:.2,h:22,p:2,ok:`{A} signs. "Your turn." Then puts {B} through the table. The table explodes. That's the image on the poster.`,g:`{A} signs, slides the contract across and says, "Your turn." The second {B} looks down, {A} is up. The table explodes. That's the image on the {PPV} poster.`,no:`{A} signs and reaches for {B}. "Come here—" {B} reverses, and {A} goes through the table instead.`,b:`{A} signs and grabs {B}. "Up you — come on — up." {A} can't lift {B}, and {B} puts {A} through the table instead. The pen rolls across the floor.`},
{key:1,t:'Add a stipulation before signing',stp:1,s:'mic',d:.15,h:15,p:3,ok:`"Before I sign this, let's make it interesting." {A} adds a stipulation and signs. The stakes just went way up. The crowd roars.`,g:`{A} picks up the pen, then stops. "One more line. When I win, you don't get a rematch. Ever." {A} signs before {B} can answer. The stakes just went way up. The crowd roars.`,no:`{A} grabs the pen. "One more clause. If either of us is counted out, the match restarts, unless the referee rules the count-out was—" {B} laughs. "Did anyone follow that?" Nobody did.`,b:`"I want to add a stipulation. That it's a match." The lawyer explains that it already is one. {B} laughs.`},
{end:1,t:'Sign it respectfully and walk away',s:'luck',d:0,h:8,p:2,ok:`{A} signs and nods to the lawyer. "Thank you." Then walks away without another word. A classy moment that makes the match feel big.`,g:`{A} signs, stands and nods once. "I'll see you there." No theatrics, and somehow that makes {PPV} feel enormous. A classy moment.`,no:`{A} signs. "See you there." And walks away. Anticlimactic. The crowd wanted a fight.`,b:`{A} signs politely. "Okay. Bye. See you." {A} walks the wrong way and has to come back past {B} to leave. Anticlimactic.`},
{ri:'brawl',end:'ok g b',t:'Both sign — then a pull-apart brawl breaks out',s:'luck',d:.05,h:14,p:2,ok:`Both sign. {A} stands. "It's done." {B} shoves them, and a pull-apart brawl breaks out. The whole locker room empties to separate them.`,g:`Both sign. Both stand. {A} leans across the table. "See you at {PPV}." Nobody moves for two seconds, then everybody does. The whole locker room empties, and {A} is still yelling the date while being dragged out.`,no:`They both sign. {A} shoves {B}. "Let's go, right now!" Security is there so fast the brawl is over before it starts.`,b:`Both sign. {A} lunges. "Come — come here!" A brawl breaks out, mostly {A} tangled in the tablecloth. The crowd laughs.`},
{al:'f',gone:'b',t:'Sign, then offer a handshake {B} won\'t take',s:'pop',d:.05,h:10,p:3,ok:`{A} signs and offers a hand. "Good luck, {B}. I mean it." {B} won't take it. {A} looks like the bigger person, and {B} looks petty.`,g:`{A} signs and offers a hand. "Whatever happens, I respect you." {B} won't take it. {A} leaves it there, perfectly still, until the crowd starts booing {B}. {B} looks petty.`,no:`{A} signs and offers a hand. "No hard feelings." {B} takes it and squeezes way too hard. {A} winces on camera.`,b:`{A} offers a hand with the pen still in it. "Good — oh. Here." {B} takes the pen, signs, and leaves with it.`},
{al:'f',vs:'h',t:'Flip the table on {B} before they can try anything',s:'ring',d:.1,h:16,p:3,ok:`{A} sees {B}'s eyes go to the table. "Don't even think about it." {A} flips it onto {B} first. The fans love it.`,g:`{A} sees {B}'s eyes move to the table. "Don't." Then flips it straight into them. {A} beat {B} to the punch, and the fans love it.`,no:`{A} grabs the table. "Not this time!" {B} was waiting for exactly that, steps aside, and the table crashes into nothing.`,b:`{A} grabs the table. "Here it — whoa." {B} is leaning on it. {A} hangs off the edge. {B} doesn't even look up.`},
{al:'h',gone:'no',t:'Refuse to sign until {B} begs',s:'mic',d:.15,h:15,p:2,ok:`"I'm not signing until you beg, {B}." {A} slides the pen away and waits. The silence stretches on, and every second of it makes {B} look smaller.`,g:`{A} holds the pen up, out of reach. "Say please. Say you need this." A long, ugly pause while the whole building waits on {B}. {B} has to stand there and take it on live TV.`,no:`{A} pushes the pen away. "Beg, {B}. On camera." {B} just stands up and leaves. Now {A} has to chase the match.`,b:`{A} folds their arms. "Beg first. Then I'll sign." {A} signs anyway out of habit before {B} answers. "Wait. No." The crowd cheers the mistake.`},
{al:'h',nhk:'chair',t:'Sign, then smash a chair across {B}\'s back',s:'ring',d:.15,h:20,p:1,ok:`{A} signs and slides the contract over. "Your turn." As {B} bends down, the chair comes across their back. Cowardly, vicious and very effective.`,g:`{A} signs, slides the paper over, and as {B} leans down to read it, the chair comes across their back. "Initial here." Cowardly, vicious and very effective.`,no:`{A} signs. "Read it carefully, {B}." {A} swings the chair, but {B} ducks and it hits the table. The contract goes flying.`,b:`{A} grabs the chair. "Sign THIS!" {A} winds up and smashes the water jug instead. Everyone gets wet. {B} is fine.`},
{al:'h',nhk:'lawyer',end:'g',t:'Slip a nasty clause into the fine print',s:'mic',d:.2,h:14,p:3,ok:`{A} slides the contract across. "Standard terms." {B} signs without reading the last line. Uh oh.`,g:`{A} smiles at {B}. "Standard terms. Totally fair." {B} signs. {A} taps one tiny line near the bottom and walks out laughing. Uh oh.`,no:`{A} pushes it over. "Just sign. It's standard." {B} reads every word, finds the clause and crosses it out right in front of {A}. "Nice try."`,b:`{A} taps the bottom of the page. "Don't — don't read this bit." {B} reads that bit. And crosses it out.`}]}},
rally:{
solo:{texts:['{A} gathers {F} in the ring for a show of force.',
 {al:'f',t:'{A} and {F} come out to a sea of their merch in the crowd.'},
 {al:'h',t:'{A} leads {F} out and they surround the ring like they own the place.'}],ch:[
{t:'Declare they will run AEW',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,ok:`"From now on, this is our company. Anybody who has a problem with that knows where to find us." Every word lands. They look dangerous.`,g:`"Look at the people next to me. Now look at who's next to you." {A} lets it sink in. "We don't want a spot on the card. We are the card." They look like the most dangerous group in the company.`,no:`{A} unfolds a list. "Goal one: titles. Goal two: respect. Goal three: a better locker room. Goal four—" The group behind {A} shifts awkwardly. They look lost.`,b:`"We will run AEW! We will run it! We'll be running it... very soon." The rest of {F} look at each other. Who wrote this?`},
{t:'Hit their music and pose',s:'pop',d:0,p:2,ok:`Their music hits. {A} raises a fist. "This is us!" They pose together in the middle of the ring. A great visual. The fans eat it up.`,g:`The music hits, the pyro fires, and the whole group stands perfectly still, arms crossed. {A} says only: "Get used to it." A great visual. The fans eat it up.`,no:`{A} points. "Pose!" Half the group goes left and half goes right. It looks unrehearsed.`,b:`The pyro misfires and somebody's coat starts smoking. {A} waves at it. "It's fine! Pose! Just pose!" They pose anyway, a little nervously.`},
{t:'Call out the entire locker room',s:'mic',d:.25,p:4,ok:`"We're calling out the whole locker room. Anybody wants it, come get it!" Bold! The roster is on notice.`,g:`"Everybody in that locker room — I don't care how long you've been here, I don't care what you've won. Come out here." Nobody does. {A} smiles. "That's what I thought." The whole roster is on notice.`,no:`{A} points at the curtain. "Whole locker room. Come on out." Nobody comes out. It just looks empty.`,b:`{A} yells at the curtain. "Everybody! Come out here!" One random wrestler walks out by mistake, waves and walks back in.`},
{t:'Tease a new member joining soon',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,ok:`"We've got someone new coming. Soon. And you'll know them when you see them." Who is it? The rumor mill is spinning.`,g:`"There's someone in this building tonight who's going to be standing here with us." {A} smiles. "And they haven't told their friends yet." The rumor mill is spinning.`,no:`{A} leans in. "Someone new is coming. Maybe soon. Maybe not. Possibly. We'll see." Nobody cares.`,b:`{A} teases it. "Someone new is joining us, and Mike's gonna — forget I said that." Nobody does.`},
{al:'f',t:'Invite a fan into the ring to pose with the group',s:'pop',d:.1,p:4,ok:`{A} waves a fan over the barricade. "Get in here! Picture time!" A moment that fan will never forget. Neither will the crowd.`,g:`{A} pulls a kid over the barricade and drapes the group's shirt over them. "Now you're one of us. Don't let anybody push you around." A moment that fan will never forget.`,no:`{A} pulls a fan into the ring. "Smile!" The fan freezes up, and security has to help them back out.`,b:`{A} picks a fan. "You! Come pose!" They're wearing a rival's shirt. Nobody notices until the photo comes up on the big screen.`},
{al:'f',t:'Promise to protect the locker room from bullies',s:'mic',d:.1,p:3,ok:`"As long as we're here, nobody gets bullied in that locker room. Nobody." The crowd is fully behind them.`,g:`"When I came up, a guy in that locker room stole my gear and told me to stay in my lane. I'm not naming names." A long look at the camera. "You know who you are. That stops now." Heroes.`,no:`"Bullying is never okay. Be kind. Respect each other." It sounds like a PSA.`,b:`"We're here to protect the locker room! From bullies. The bully ones." It sounds like a PSA read by someone who skimmed it.`},
{al:'h',t:'Beat down a local enhancement talent to send a message',s:'ring',d:.05,p:2,ok:`{F} take the local wrestler apart. {A} stands over them. "Tell the locker room what happened here." Message received. The locker room is scared.`,g:`{F} take the local wrestler apart. {A} crouches by the corner camera: "That's not a match. That was a memo." Message received. The locker room is scared.`,no:`{A} points at the local wrestler. "Take him apart." The local wrestler fights back for a while. It's embarrassing, even after they win.`,b:`{A} waves the group in. "Get him! ...A little help here? Guys?" The local wrestler nearly wins.`},
{al:'h',t:'Unveil matching gear and declare the belts are next',s:'mic',d:.1,p:3,ok:`They unveil matching gear and point at the tag titles. "Those are next." They look like a real threat — and very well dressed.`,g:`The matching gear goes on. {A} points at the tag belts hanging on the stage. "We bought the outfits. Now we're going shopping." They look like a real threat — and very well dressed.`,no:`{A} unzips the matching jacket. "We look the part. The belts are next." The gear doesn't fit. Half of it is too tight, and the crowd notices.`,b:`{A} holds up the gear. "Our colors!" It's the wrong team's colors. "...The belts are next anyway." Nobody can take them seriously.`}]},
duo:{texts:['{A} and {B} stand side by side in the ring.',
 {al:'f',t:'{A} and {B} come out together to a huge ovation.'},
 {al:'h',t:'{A} and {B} stand in the ring, arms folded, staring down the crowd.'}],ch:[
{t:'"We are the future of this company."',s:'mic',d:.1,p:3,c:2,ok:`"We are the future of this company. Get used to it." They look like a unit fans will follow.`,g:`"Everybody keeps asking who's next." {A} looks at {B}. {B} looks back. "You're looking at it." They look like a unit fans will follow.`,no:`{A} and {B} both start. "We are the future—" They stop. Both start again. "We are the—" Awkward.`,b:`"We are the — " "— future of —" "No, you go." "No, you." The crowd starts counting.`},
{t:'Pose together to a huge reaction',s:'pop',d:.05,p:2,c:1,ok:`{A} nudges {B}. "Now." They pose together. The chemistry is obvious.`,g:`They hit the pose together without even looking at each other. {A}, barely moving their lips: "Told you." The chemistry is obvious.`,no:`{A} counts it off. "Three, two, one—" {B} poses a second late. Mild reaction at best.`,b:`{A} calls it. "Pose!" They go in completely different directions. "Again!" Then a third time. Mild reaction at best.`},
{t:'Name their next target',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,c:1,ok:`"We're coming for the tag team champions. And we're not asking nicely." Somebody in the back just got nervous.`,g:`"We could name the whole division. We're not going to." {A} smiles. "One of you is going to get home tonight and find out it's you." Somebody in the back just got nervous.`,no:`{A} points. "We're coming for the champions. And the number one contenders. And the team after that." The threat sounds hollow.`,b:`{A} points. "We're coming for the Wolf Brothers!" Someone in the crowd yells "They're gone!"`},
{t:'Debut a new double-team finisher on a local wrestler',s:'ring',d:.1,p:3,c:1,ok:`{A} hooks the local wrestler. "Now!" The new double-team finisher. The local wrestler does not get up. The crowd is impressed.`,g:`{A} looks at {B}. "Show them." The double team is crisp, brand new and brutal, and the referee counts three before the local wrestler knows what happened.`,no:`{A} calls it. "Now! No — wait—" They miscommunicate, and the local wrestler nearly steals a pin.`,b:`{A} yells "NOW!" The new finisher hits {B} instead. The local wrestler pins them both. Almost.`},
{al:'f',t:'Celebrate with the fans at ringside',s:'pop',d:.05,p:3,c:1,ok:`{A} leaps the barricade. "Come here, everybody!" Hugs, high fives and selfies. Pure joy.`,g:`They leap the barricade together. {A} tosses a sweaty headband to a kid. "That's yours." Hugs, high fives and selfies. Pure joy.`,no:`{A} hops the barricade. "Who wants a high five?" They get swarmed. Security pulls them back.`,b:`{A} hops the barricade. "Hi! Hi! {B}? Where'd you go?" They come back separately. One of them is missing a shoe.`},
{al:'f',t:'Promise to always have each other\'s back',s:'mic',d:.1,p:2,c:2,ok:`"No matter what happens, I've got your back. Always." The fans believe them. Now these two feel like family.`,g:`{A} puts an arm around {B}. "I've had partners who left. I've had partners who lied. I'm not saying this one's different." A smile. "I'm saying I'd bet everything on it." Now these two feel like family.`,no:`{A} grips {B}'s shoulder. "I'll always have your back. Always. No matter what. Even when it hurts. Especially then." Something about it feels like foreshadowing.`,b:`"I'll always have your back." "And I'll always have your... back too." It sounds like they've never met. Foreshadowing.`},
{al:'h',t:'Declare the rest of the division beneath them',s:'mic',d:.1,p:2,c:1,ok:`"Nobody in this division can touch us. Nobody." Arrogant and united. Everyone wants to see them humbled.`,g:`"We looked at the rankings. We laughed. We looked again. Still laughing." {A} shrugs. "Nobody in this division is a challenge. They're a schedule." Arrogant and united.`,no:`{A} sneers. "This division is beneath us." {B} cuts in: "I said that first." They argue about who said it first.`,b:`"The division is beneath us." {B} nods: "Under us." {A} again: "Lower than us." {B}: "...Yeah." The crowd starts to giggle.`},
{al:'h',t:'Blindside a random wrestler to show what they can do',s:'ring',d:.1,p:2,c:2,ok:`{A} nods at {B}. "Him." They blindside a random wrestler. A ruthless display of teamwork.`,g:`They blindside a wrestler who was just walking past. As they stroll off, {A} yells to the back: "That's what happens when you're in the hallway." A ruthless display of teamwork.`,no:`{A} points. "That one." The wrestler gets a few licks in first, and it takes both of them too long.`,b:`{A} points. "Get him!" He's much bigger than they expected. "...Never mind." They retreat.`}]}},
champ:{
solo:{texts:['{A} walks out with the {T} title over their shoulder.',
 {al:'f',t:'{A} holds the {T} title up to every side of the arena as the fans cheer.'},
 {al:'h',t:'{A} strolls out polishing the {T} title and refuses to let anyone near it.'}],ch:[
{t:'Declare themselves the greatest {T} champion ever',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,ok:`"I'm the greatest {T} champion this company has ever had. Look it up." Nobody's arguing tonight.`,g:`"There've been a lot of {T} champions. Good ones. Great ones." {A} lifts the belt. "And every one of them, when I'm done, will be the answer to a trivia question." Nobody is arguing tonight.`,no:`{A} lifts the belt. "Greatest {T} champion ever. Say it." The crowd starts chanting someone else's name.`,b:`"I'm the greatest champion of all time! Of the... {T}. Of this belt. Ever. Probably." The crowd chants for someone else.`},
{t:'Promise to defend against anyone, any time',s:'pop',d:.05,p:3,ok:`"Anybody wants this title, it's right here. Any time, anywhere." A fighting champion. The fans love it.`,g:`"Anyone. Any time. I don't need a week's notice. I don't need a contract." {A} holds the belt up. "I need you to show up." A fighting champion. The fans love it.`,no:`"I'll defend against anybody, whenever, wherever, for whatever." It rings hollow. Everybody knows how that's gone before.`,b:`"I'll fight anyone, anytime, any... where..." {A} looks to the back, nervous someone might actually come out. It rings hollow.`},
{t:'Hold the title high and let the crowd react',s:'pop',d:.1,p:2,ok:`{A} raises the title high. "This is what it's all for." A goosebumps moment.`,g:`{A} raises the belt and turns slowly in a full circle, so every seat gets to see it. Only then: "Still mine." A goosebumps moment.`,no:`{A} holds the title up. "Let me hear it!" The reaction is mixed.`,b:`{A} lifts the belt. "Behold the — hang on." It slips off one shoulder, then the other. They hold it upside down for a second. The reaction is mixed.`},
{t:'Show a highlight reel of every title defense',s:'luck',d:0,p:2,ok:`{A} points at the screen. "Watch. Every defense." The reel plays. A reminder of how dominant this reign has been.`,g:`Defense after defense on the big screen, every one ending with {A} standing tall. When it's over, {A} says one word into the mic: "Next." A reminder of how dominant this reign has been.`,no:`{A} points at the screen. "Roll it." The reel drags, the music is too loud, and it's hard to tell which match is which.`,b:`{A} points at the screen. "Roll my greatest moments!" It's mostly bloopers. "Who edited this?" {A} watches themselves fall off the top rope.`},
{al:'f',t:'Dedicate the title to the fans',s:'pop',d:.05,p:3,ok:`"This belongs to all of you. I just get to carry it." Huge pop.`,g:`{A} walks to the barricade and holds the belt out to the front row. "Touch it. Go on. It's yours too. I just carry it." Huge pop.`,no:`{A} holds up the belt. "This is for all of you." Sweet, but the crowd wanted fire.`,b:`"This title is for all of you. You can't have it, though." A beat. "But it's for you." The crowd isn't sure what they've been given.`},
{al:'f',t:'Name every top contender and promise to face them all',s:'mic',d:.1,p:3,ok:`{A} names every top contender. "One at a time, or all at once. I'll face every one of you." The roster takes notice.`,g:`{A} goes down the list, every contender by name. "You, because you're fast. You, because you're mean. You, because you think you're ready." Then: "I'll beat every one of you." The roster takes notice.`,no:`{A} goes down the list. "There's — the tall one. And, uh, the one with the jacket." {A} forgets half the names.`,b:`{A} names the contenders. "And Dave, from the third row!" Dave is a fan. He stands up and bows.`},
{al:'h',t:'Insult the whole roster while polishing the belt',s:'mic',d:.1,p:2,ok:`{A} polishes the belt. "Overrated. Injured. Lazy. Nobody." Everyone in the back wants a piece of {A} now.`,g:`{A} polishes the belt slowly, never looking up. "Overrated. Injured. Lazy. Who? Who? Overrated." Each one a name in the back. Everyone wants a piece of {A} now.`,no:`{A} polishes the belt. "And another thing about the roster—" More polishing. "Where was I?" The crowd isn't sure what the point was.`,b:`{A} polishes away. "Lazy. Overrated. And my tag partner, who's the worst of all—" The partner, at ringside, looks hurt.`},
{al:'h',t:'Declare there are no worthy challengers left',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,ok:`"There's nobody left. I've beaten everybody worth beating." Arrogant, maddening and completely convincing.`,g:`"I've looked. I've honestly looked." {A} turns to the stage, waits. "Nobody. Not one of you." Arrogant, maddening and completely convincing.`,no:`{A} spreads their arms. "There's nobody left!" A dozen wrestlers walk out to disagree.`,b:`"There are no worthy challengers left!" A wrestler walks out. "...Except maybe that one. And I'll beat them too." The crowd laughs.`},
{al:'h',t:'Demand a raise from Tony Khan on live TV',s:'mic',d:.2,p:4,ok:`"Tony Khan, I'm the champion. I carry this place. Pay me what I'm worth!" The boos turn into laughter. The most entertaining jerk in the company.`,g:`{A} looks straight into the camera. "Tony. Tony. I know you're watching. I carry this company. I want it in writing by Wednesday." A pause. "And I want it in cash." The boos turn into laughter.`,no:`{A} faces the camera. "Tony, industry rates for a champion of my caliber are, frankly, well above—" It drags. {A} looks petty.`,b:`"Tony, I want a raise. A big one. Like, ten — no, twenty percent." The crowd chants "Thirty!" {A} takes it.`}]},
duo:{texts:['{A} holds the {T} title high — and {B} walks out to stare at it.',
 {al:'h',vs:'f',t:'{A} is mid-gloat about the {T} title when {B}\'s music hits to a huge roar.'},
 {al:'f',vs:'h',t:'{B} interrupts {A}\'s celebration, eyeing the {T} title hungrily.'}],ch:[
{t:'Tell {B} to earn a title shot first',s:'mic',d:.1,h:12,p:2,ok:`"You want this? Go earn it first. You haven't done anything to deserve a title shot." {B} is fuming. Now they have a mission.`,g:`"You want a shot? Everybody wants a shot." {A} taps the belt. "Go win something, {B}. Anything. Then knock on my door." {B} is fuming. Now they have a mission.`,no:`{A} taps the belt. "Earn it first." {B} counts it off. "Six straight wins. Two over people you ducked." {B} gets the upper hand.`,b:`"You have to earn a shot! Like I did." {B} reminds everyone how {A} actually won it. {A} has no answer.`},
{t:'Grant {B} a title match on the spot',s:'pop',d:.05,h:10,p:3,ok:`"You want a title shot, {B}? You've got one." Huge pop. Everyone wants to see it.`,g:`"You want it? Fine." {A} holds the belt out. "But when I beat you, you go to the back of the line and you stay there." The crowd erupts. Everyone wants to see it.`,no:`{A} shrugs. "Sure. You want a shot, you've got one." It feels too easy. Nobody's sure why {A} agreed.`,b:`{A} nods. "You've got a title match! Wait — no. Hang on." Too late. The crowd already cheered.`},
{al:'h',t:'Nail {B} with the title belt',s:'ring',d:.15,h:18,p:1,ok:`{A} swings the belt into {B}. "Keep your hands off my gold." {B} is down, and the gold is back on {A}'s shoulder.`,g:`{A} lets {B} talk, nods, then swings the belt flush. As {B} drops, {A} drapes it back over {A}'s own shoulder. "That's as close as you get." The gold is back where it belongs.`,no:`{A} cocks the belt back. "You want this?" {B} ducks it, and {A} eats a superkick.`,b:`{A} swings the belt. "Take — whoops." {A} lets go of it, and it flies into the crowd. {B} superkicks {A}.`},
{al:'h',gone:'b',ri:'belt',t:'Hand {B} the belt — let them feel what they\'ll never have',s:'mic',d:.1,h:14,p:2,ok:`"Go on. Hold it. Feel what you'll never have." {B} holds it a little too long. The tension is thick.`,g:`{A} hands {B} the belt. "Feel the weight. Remember it." {B} holds it a little too long. {A} smiles. "That's the closest you'll ever get to it." The tension is thick.`,no:`{A} hands it over. "Feel what you'll never have." {B} won't give it back. Now {A} looks foolish, standing there with an empty shoulder.`,b:`{A} hands {B} the belt. {B} walks off with it. {A} chases after them up the ramp, yelling "Hey!"`},
{al:'f',t:'Shake {B}\'s hand — champion to challenger',s:'pop',d:.05,h:8,p:3,ok:`"Champion to challenger. Let's give them a good one." They shake hands. Respect, and a match that suddenly feels huge.`,g:`{A} holds out a hand. "Champion to challenger. Best one I've had." {B} shakes it. {A} holds the grip a second longer. "Doesn't mean you win." Respect, and a match that suddenly feels huge.`,no:`{A} offers a hand. "Champion to challenger." {B} ignores it. Cold.`,b:`{A} offers a hand. "Champion to — oh, we're hugging?" {B} goes for the shake, {A} goes for a hug. They end up in a weird half-embrace.`},
{al:'f',vs:'h',t:'Tell {B} they\'ll never win this title by cheating',s:'mic',d:.1,h:12,p:2,ok:`"You'll never win this title by cheating, {B}. Not while I'm champion." The fans are fully behind the champion.`,g:`"Here's what's going to happen, {B}. You'll cheat. You'll do everything you always do. And at the end of it, I'll still be holding this." The fans are fully behind the champion.`,no:`{A} wags a finger. "Cheaters never hold this belt." {B} smirks. "Remember the low blow at Revolution? I do." A few past "accidents" on {A}'s record come up.`,b:`"You'll never win this by cheating! Cheaters never win. Usually." {B} lists times cheaters won. It's a long list.`},
{al:'h',t:'Make {B} kneel before the title',s:'mic',d:.15,h:16,p:2,ok:`"Get on your knees and show this title some respect, {B}." {B} refuses, and the confrontation boils over.`,g:`"Kneel." {A} holds the belt out at waist height. "Not for me. For it. Show it some respect for once." {B} refuses, and the confrontation boils over.`,no:`{A} points down. "Kneel." {B} just laughs. "Make me." The demand looks silly.`,b:`"Kneel! Kneel before — before the title. Kneel." {B} sits down cross-legged instead. The crowd loves it.`},
{al:'h',t:'Hide behind the referee and taunt {B}',s:'luck',d:.05,h:12,p:1,ok:`{A} ducks behind the referee. "Go on, {B}. Hit a ref on TV." Cowardly champion 101. The crowd is furious.`,g:`{A} slides behind the referee and peeks around the ref's shoulder. "Hit me, {B}. Go ahead. Hit a referee on live TV." A smile. "I'll wait." Cowardly champion 101. The crowd is furious.`,no:`{A} slides behind the ref. "Try it, {B}. I dare you—" The ref steps aside, and {A} has to scramble out of reach.`,b:`{A} crouches behind the referee. "Can't touch me now!" The referee is much shorter than {A}. Nobody is hidden. The ref steps aside.`}]}},
turn:{
solo:{texts:[{al:'f',t:'{A} walks out to a big pop, but something is off. No smile. No high-fives.'},
 {al:'h',t:'{A} comes out alone, without the usual sneer. The boos slowly fade into curious murmurs.'}],ch:[
{al:'f',t:'Blame the fans for every loss',s:'mic',d:.1,p:3,ok:`"You know what? Every time I lost, you were there cheering somebody else. I'm done caring what you think." The cheers turn into boos.`,g:`"Every time I lost, you were sad for about ten minutes. Then you went home." {A} looks out at them. "I didn't. I lived in it. You never once gave me anything back." The cheers curdle into boos.`,no:`{A} reads from a phone. "Every time I lost, you weren't there for me." Nobody quite buys it yet.`,b:`"It's your fault! All of you! You... cheered too hard. For me. And that's — that's on you." Nobody quite buys it.`},
{al:'f',t:'Slowly take off the old gear and throw it into the crowd',s:'pop',d:.05,p:3,ok:`{A} peels off the old gear and throws it into the crowd. "Keep it. I won't need it." A chilling image. The new {A} has arrived.`,g:`{A} peels off the old gear one piece at a time, never looking at the crowd, and drops each piece over the ropes. The last one, {A} holds up. "That person's gone." A chilling image. The new {A} has arrived.`,no:`{A} hurls the old gear into the crowd. "That's the past!" A fan throws it right back.`,b:`{A} pulls at the old shirt. "That person is — hold on — is GONE —" Arms stuck over their head for a full minute. A fan throws it back.`},
{al:'f',t:'Announce they\'re done playing nice — and mean it',s:'mic',d:.05,p:2,ok:`"I'm done playing nice. From now on, it's about me." Short, cold and effective.`,g:`"I was nice. For years. I held doors. I took the losses. I said thank you." {A} smiles, and it isn't a nice smile. "You're welcome." Short, cold and effective.`,no:`{A} grips the mic. "I'm done playing nice, and here's why. When I first got here, I—" The mic cuts out halfway through.`,b:`"I'm done playing nice! From now on I'm gonna be... not nice. Mean. Meaner." The crowd isn't sure what changed.`},
{al:'h',t:'Apologize to the fans — with feeling',s:'mic',d:.15,p:4,ok:`"I've said a lot of things about you people. I was wrong. I'm sorry." The building believes it. A new hero is born.`,g:`"I said things about you that weren't true. I said them because they got a reaction." {A} takes a breath. "I'd like a different reaction now. I'll earn it." The building believes every word. A new hero is born.`,no:`{A} reads from a card. "I regret any statements that may have caused offense to any persons in attendance." It sounds like it went through a lawyer. The fans are skeptical.`,b:`"I'm sorry. To the fans. For the — the things. You know." Nobody knows. The fans are skeptical.`},
{al:'h',t:'Tear up their old catchphrase shirt',s:'pop',d:.05,p:3,ok:`{A} holds up the old catchphrase shirt. "That's not me anymore." Tears it in half. A clean break with the past. Huge reaction.`,g:`{A} holds up the old shirt with the catchphrase on it, reads it out loud one last time, then tears it straight down the middle. "Never again." A clean break. Huge reaction.`,no:`{A} grips the shirt. "Never ag— come on." It won't rip. {A} tugs for a while, then just throws it. Awkward.`,b:`{A} grips the shirt. "Never — again — rip, you —" {A} tries to bite it. A fan hands them scissors.`},
{al:'h',t:'Invite a fan into the ring for a hug',s:'luck',d:0,p:2,ok:`{A} waves a fan over the barricade. "Come here. Thank you for believing in me." A hug. Pure feel-good television.`,g:`{A} waves a kid over the barricade, kneels and opens their arms. "I'm sorry I wasn't who you wanted. I am now." The kid runs in. {A} holds on a long time.`,no:`{A} reaches out. "Come here." The fan flinches. Old habits. The hug happens, but stiffly.`,b:`{A} opens their arms. "Hug it out!" The fan goes for a high five. They end up in a sort of headlock. Old habits.`}]},
duo:{texts:[{al:'f',t:'{A} comes out to stand beside {B}. The crowd cheers the pair — they have no idea what\'s coming.'},
 {al:'h',t:'{B} is in trouble in the ring, and {A} is watching from the ramp…'}],ch:[
{al:'f',t:'Low blow {B} out of nowhere',s:'ring',d:0,h:14,p:2,ok:`{A} turns, and the low blow comes from nowhere. "Surprise." {A} stands tall over {B}. Shock and outrage.`,g:`{A} offers a hand, {B} reaches for it, and the low blow comes from nowhere. {A} stands over {B} and finally says it: "You never saw me coming. Nobody ever does." Shock and outrage.`,no:`{A} goes low. "Never saw it c—" {B} blocks it, but the turn is done. {A} walks off anyway.`,b:`{A} winds up. "Here's what I think of — oh." {B} blocks it. {A} keeps walking away like it worked. The turn is done.`},
{al:'f',t:'Hit {B} with a chair and walk off smiling',s:'ring',d:.1,h:18,p:3,ok:`The chair comes down. {A} drops it on {B}'s chest. "We're done." Walks off smiling. Fans are furious and glued to their screens.`,g:`The chair comes down once. {A} drops it on {B}'s chest. "Thanks for everything." Then walks up the ramp smiling, waving like nothing happened. Fans are furious.`,no:`{A} swings the chair. "We're done, {B}." It's soft, but the message is clear. {A} walks off.`,b:`{A} swings the chair. "We're — ow, my foot." It barely connects, and {A} drops it on their own foot. Still, the message is clear.`},
{al:'f',t:'Explain, calmly, why {B} was always holding them back',s:'mic',d:.15,h:12,p:3,ok:`"You held me back, {B}. For years. I'm done carrying you." Cold and calculated. The betrayal cuts deep.`,g:`"I carried you. Every match. Every promo. Every bad night." {A} speaks quietly over {B}. "And every time, they said your name first. Not anymore." Cold and calculated. The betrayal cuts deep.`,no:`{A} stands over {B}. "There was the match in Boston. And the one in Tampa. And the tag title shot we should have had—" It rambles, but the damage is done.`,b:`"You were holding me back! With your... holding. Back." {A} looks down at {B}. The damage is done anyway.`},
{al:'h',t:'Run in and make the save for {B}',s:'ring',d:0,h:4,p:3,c:2,ok:`{A} hits the ring. "Not on my watch!" The building explodes. {A} and {B} stand tall together.`,g:`{A}'s music hits and the building comes unglued. {A} clears the ring, then turns, looks at {B} and offers a hand. "About time." The building explodes. They stand tall together.`,no:`{A} slides in a step late. "Back off!" The intent is clear. They stand together.`,b:`{A} slides in way too early. "I'm here! Oh. Not yet?" {A} waits for the attack to actually start. The intent is still clear.`},
{al:'h',t:'Refuse to attack {B} when told to',s:'mic',d:.1,h:6,p:4,ok:`{A} is handed the chair. Looks at {B}. "No." The chair hits the mat. The fans chant {A}'s name.`,g:`{A} is handed the chair. Looks at it. Looks at {B}. Looks back at the crowd. "No." The chair hits the mat. A powerful moment of defiance. The fans chant {A}'s name.`,no:`{A} holds the chair a long time. "I... I can't. I won't." It's muddled, but the crowd gets it.`,b:`"I won't do it! I will not hit {B}." {A} accidentally bumps into {B}. "That doesn't count." The crowd gets it, mostly.`},
{al:'h',t:'Shake {B}\'s hand in front of everyone',s:'pop',d:.05,h:2,p:3,c:3,ok:`{A} holds out a hand. "I was wrong about you." {B} shakes it. Respect earned. The fans are all in.`,g:`{A} crosses the ring and holds out a hand in front of everyone. "I was wrong about you. Took me too long to say it." {B} shakes it. Respect earned. The fans are all in.`,no:`{A} offers a hand. "I owe you this." {B} leaves {A} hanging — for now.`,b:`{A} offers a hand. "I was wrong about — this hand. No, this one." {B} leaves them hanging, for now.`}]}},
vignette:{
solo:{texts:[{t:'The cameras catch {A} backstage.',kk:'tape back'},
 {kk:'tape dayoff',t:'The cameras follow {A} through a day off.'},
 {kk:'tape trespass',al:'h',t:'A shaky camera finds {A} somewhere they definitely shouldn\'t be.'}],ch:[
{t:'A gritty training montage',s:'ring',d:0,p:2,ok:`Early mornings, heavy weights, a punishing ring session. {A}, dripping, to the lens: "Every day. No days off." They look ready for war.`,g:`Five a.m., an empty gym, the same drill a hundred times. At the end, {A} looks at the lens, out of breath: "This is the part nobody claps for." They look ready for war.`,no:`Weights, ropes, a sunrise run. {A} to camera: "I'm working harder than ever." It looks like every other montage.`,b:`The montage cuts to {A} talking to camera. "I train because — because the training is — what was the question?" The editor leaves it in.`},
{t:'A comedic bit with the production crew',s:'mic',d:.2,p:4,ok:`{A} hands a camera operator a clipboard. "You're my new manager. First rule: never film my left side." The internet is going to love this one.`,g:`{A} spends a full minute dead serious, explaining to a terrified camera operator why it matters which way the logo faces. The operator flips it. {A} nods. "Thank you." The internet is going to love this one.`,no:`{A} starts a bit with the sound guy. "So I says to him, I says—" It goes on too long and dies. Crickets.`,b:`{A} giggles. "Okay, okay, so the punchline is — wait, I need to set it up first. Hold on." Crickets.`},
{t:'A dark, cryptic message',s:'mic',d:.15,p:3,ok:`A dark, cryptic message in a shadowy room. "It's coming. You won't see it until it's too late." Everyone is talking about what it means.`,g:`A single candle. {A}'s voice, barely above a whisper: "Four. Then three. You'll know when it's two." The candle goes out. Everyone is talking about what it means.`,no:`{A} in a shadowy room. "The raven flies at midnight. The tide turns on the fourth. Seek the key where the clock stops—" It's confusing rather than intriguing.`,b:`"The darkness is coming. The darkness. It's... it's dark." A light is clearly visible behind them. Confusing.`},
{nhk:'roof|car|school|gym|arena|truck|stage|study',t:'A slow-motion walk through the parking garage',s:'pop',d:.05,p:2,ok:`Slow motion through the parking garage, music swelling. {A}, without breaking stride: "Let's go." Cinematic and cool. Pure star power.`,g:`Slow motion, steam rising from the vents, {A} walking dead center past every car. At the end, a glance over the shoulder: "See you Sunday." Pure star power.`,no:`The slow-motion walk goes on and on. {A}, finally: "I'm ready." A lens flare in every shot. It looks like a car commercial.`,b:`Slow motion through the garage. {A}: "It's time." A car honks at {A} to get out of the way. "...Sorry!" They keep it in.`},
{nhk:'back|car|trespass|school|arena|gym|roof|truck|stage|study',al:'f',t:'Visit a children\'s hospital',s:'pop',d:.05,p:4,ok:`{A} hands out signed photos on a children's ward. "Who's the toughest one here? You? I believe it." Heartwarming. A hero in and out of the ring.`,g:`{A} sits on the floor of a children's ward playing cards, losing on purpose, for an hour. "Okay, you win again. Best of fifty?" One kid tells the camera {A} is bad at cards. Heartwarming.`,no:`{A} sits with the kids. "You're all champions to me." A lovely moment, but it airs during a commercial break and nobody sees it.`,b:`{A} reads a book to the kids. "The very hung— hungry — caterp—" The kids read it back to {A}. Lovely, anyway.`},
{hk:'back|arena',al:'f',t:'Help the ring crew set up after hours',s:'pop',d:0,p:2,ok:`{A} carries ring steps with the crew after hours. "These people built my career. I can carry a chair." The crew adores {A}.`,g:`Midnight, empty arena. {A} carries steps and folds chairs with the ring crew, then sits on the apron with them eating cold pizza. "These people built my career. I can carry a chair." A humble, hardworking star.`,no:`{A} grabs a turnbuckle. "I've got this one — AH." Dropped on their foot. {A} spends the rest of the vignette limping around.`,b:`{A} rigs the ropes. "Top one, middle one, bottom — or is it —" Wrong order. The crew politely redoes it after.`},
{hk:'back',al:'h',t:'Trash the catering table',s:'luck',d:0,p:2,ok:`{A} sweeps the catering table onto the floor. "Nobody eats till I say so." Walks off with a cookie. Petty destruction at its finest.`,g:`{A} lifts the catering table, looks into the camera, and says: "Somebody told me the vegans get the good stuff." Then flips it. Petty destruction at its finest.`,no:`{A} grabs the catering table. "This is what I think of—" The caterer chases {A} off with a ladle before it even tips.`,b:`{A} grabs the table. "This is what I think of — whoa!" Slips on a grape. The caterer chases them off with a ladle.`},
{al:'h',t:'Stare into the camera until it cuts away',s:'mic',d:.1,p:3,ok:`{A} stares into the camera, silent. Then, very quietly: "Soon." The director cuts away. Unsettling. Nobody at home can look away.`,g:`{A} stares into the lens. Ten seconds. Twenty. At forty, a tiny smile. At sixty, a whisper: "I can see you too." The camera cuts away. Nobody at home can look away.`,no:`{A} stares into the camera. A long time. "...Soon." It goes on so long it becomes a meme — the wrong kind.`,b:`{A} stares at the camera. "...Ah-CHOO." Then keeps staring. It becomes a meme, the wrong kind.`},
{hk:'back',al:'h',t:'Threaten the backstage interviewer',s:'mic',d:.05,p:2,ok:`{A} backs the interviewer into the wall. "Ask me another stupid question. Go on." The interviewer is shaking. The fans are fuming.`,g:`{A} takes the mic from the interviewer and hands it back, slowly. "Ask me that again. I want to hear you say it." The interviewer can't. The fans are fuming.`,no:`{A} backs the interviewer against the wall. "Ask me another one. I dare you." The interviewer rolls their eyes and walks off. {A} is left yelling at nobody.`,b:`{A} threatens the interviewer, who isn't scared at all. "Are we done?" {A} nods. They're done.`}]},
duo:{texts:[{t:'The cameras catch {A} bumping into {B} backstage.',kk:'tape back'},
 {kk:'tape back door',al:'h',vs:'f',t:'{A} is waiting outside {B}\'s locker room door.'},
 {kk:'tape back catering',al:'f',vs:'f',t:'{A} and {B} run into each other at catering.'}],ch:[
{nhk:'absent',t:'A heated shoving match',s:'ring',d:.05,h:12,p:1,ok:`{A} shoves {B} into the lockers. "Say it again." {B} shoves back. "Gladly." Officials have to pull them apart.`,g:`One shove. Then a second. {A} leans in, nose to nose. "You don't scare me." {B} doesn't blink. "I should." Somebody throws a punch and officials have to pull them apart.`,no:`{A} squares up. "You and me, right n—" Security breaks it up before it gets going.`,b:`{A} shoves {B} into a wall. "How do you like — whoa!" A door opens and {A} falls into the next room. Security breaks it up.`},
{nhk:'absent',end:'ok g',t:'Cryptic mind games',s:'mic',d:.15,h:10,p:2,ok:`"Think about it, {B}. Think about what's coming." {A} smiles and walks away. {B} walks off shaken.`,g:`{A} leans in close to {B}. "You've been sleeping okay? I haven't. I keep thinking about how it ends." {A} pats {B}'s shoulder and walks off. {B} walks off shaken.`,no:`{A} tries the mind games, but {B} doesn't take the bait. "Are you done?"`,b:`"You're gonna lose and you know it, I know it, the — everybody knows it. Think about that." {B} doesn't take the bait.`},
{nhk:'absent',t:'A surprising show of respect',s:'mic',d:.1,p:3,c:2,ok:`"Hey, {B}. I don't say this often. You're good. Real good." Could this be an alliance in the making?`,g:`{A} stops {B} in the hallway. "I've never said this to anybody. You're the best I've seen." A pause. "Don't make me say it twice." Could this be an alliance in the making?`,no:`{A} clears their throat. "{B}. I respect you. As a competitor. And as a person." It comes out so stiff and rehearsed that it reads as fake.`,b:`"You're good, {B}. Like — good. Not as good as me. But good." It reads as fake.`},
{hk:'back',t:'A long, tense elevator ride together',s:'mic',d:.1,h:9,p:2,ok:`The doors close. {A} stares straight ahead. "Long way down." {B} doesn't answer. Twelve floors of silence. Nobody needs to say more.`,g:`The doors close. Neither of them speaks. On the eleventh floor, {A} reaches over and presses every button below. "Take your time getting there." {B} just watches the numbers. Nobody needs to say more.`,no:`{A} glares at {B}. "Going down." The elevator music undercuts the tension, and the cameraman's reflection is in every shot.`,b:`{A} leans in. "When those doors open, you're gonna—" Ding. "—gonna—" Ding. The elevator chimes over the punchline. Twice.`},
{hk:'catering|train',nhk:'absent',al:'f',vs:'f',t:'Friendly trash talk over a game of cards',s:'mic',d:.1,h:6,p:3,c:1,ok:`{A} shuffles the deck. "I'm beating you here and at {PPV}." Fun, loose and a little competitive.`,g:`"You can't bluff, {B}. You touch your ear." {B} lays down a full house. {A} stares. "...You touch your ear when you're winning, too?" Fun, loose and a little competitive. The fans love these two.`,no:`{A} deals. "Lost again last week, huh, {B}? Must be a habit." {B} sets down the cards. "Funny." Things get chilly fast.`,b:`{A} slaps down a pair of twos. "Read 'em and weep!" {B} lays down a flush. {A} keeps going. "Lucky! Again!" Loses every hand, keeps trash talking. It gets uncomfortable.`},
{hk:'catering',al:'f',vs:'h',gone:'ok g b',t:'Catch {B} cheating at cards in catering',s:'luck',d:.05,h:10,p:2,ok:`{A} catches {B} with an ace up the sleeve. "Some things never change." {B} storms off.`,g:`{A} flips {B}'s hand over: three aces up the sleeve. "Some things never change." {A} takes the pot and slides it to the caterer. {B} storms off.`,no:`{A} points across the table. "You've got an ace up your sleeve!" {B} shows both empty sleeves. "Prove it." {A} can't prove a thing.`,b:`{A} slams the table. "Cheater! That's an ace!" {B} points at {A}'s hand. "That one's yours." {B} pockets the rest of the pot and leaves.`},
{hk:'door|back',nhk:'absent',al:'h',vs:'f',gone:1,t:'Lock {B} in the locker room before their match',s:'luck',d:.05,h:13,p:1,ok:`{A} turns the key. "Good luck out there, {B}." {B} is banging on the door as the show goes on. Dastardly.`,g:`{A} clicks the lock, pockets the key and walks past the camera. "Shame. I heard it was a big match." {B} is banging on the door as the show goes on. Dastardly.`,no:`{A} locks the door. "Enjoy the view from in there." By the time {A} gets back, the window is open and {B} is gone.`,b:`{A} slams the door. "Nobody's going anywhere!" Click. {A} is on the wrong side of it, locked in with {B}. Long pause. {B} climbs out the window.`},
{al:'h',nhk:'absent',t:'Steal {B}\'s entrance jacket',s:'luck',d:0,h:10,p:2,ok:`{A} holds up {B}'s entrance jacket and slips it on. "Looks better on me." Later, {A} wears it to the ring. Petty and perfect.`,g:`Later in the night, {A} walks to the ring in {B}'s entrance jacket, sleeves rolled up, popping the collar. "Fits better on a champion." Petty and perfect.`,no:`{A} pulls on {B}'s jacket. "Perfect fit." The sleeves stop halfway up the forearms. They wear it anyway.`,b:`{A} shrugs on the stolen jacket. "Look at me, I'm {B} — " The shoulder seam rips. "...On purpose. That was on purpose."`}]}}};
const TWISTS=[
{hk:'live',when:'any',atk:1,text:'The crowd erupts into a chant for {A}.',ch:[{t:'Feed off the crowd',ok:`{A} paces the ring, pumping a fist with the chant. "LOUDER!" The building gets louder.`,g:`{A} lowers the mic and lets the chant wash over them, then lifts it again: "You hear that? That's why I'm still here." The building gets louder.`,no:`{A} cups an ear. "Come on, keep it going!" The chant fades before they can use it.`,b:`{A} restarts the chant themselves. "Let's go {A}! Let's go—" Way too fast. Nobody can keep up. It fades.`,s:'pop',d:.05,p:3},{t:'Tell them to shut up',ok:`"Shut up! All of you!" The chant gets louder. That's the point.`,g:`{A} waits for the loudest moment. "Shut. Up." The chant gets louder. {A} smiles. "Thank you. Exactly what I wanted." Pure heat.`,no:`{A} snaps. "Shut up! I said SHUT UP!" They just keep going. {A} looks rattled.`,b:`"Shut up! Shut — please be quiet." They get louder. {A} looks rattled.`,s:'mic',d:.15,p:2,h:3},{t:'Stay focused',ok:`{A} lets the chant roll past. "As I was saying." Business as usual.`,g:`{A} doesn't even look up. Waits for the chant to pass, then: "—and that's exactly why I'll win." Picks up mid-sentence, like nothing happened. Focused and dangerous.`,no:`{A} pushes on. "So, like I said, at {PPV} I'm going to—" The chant comes back. "—where was I?"`,b:`{A} stays locked in. "And another thing. The thing is. The..." {A} has completely forgotten what they were saying.`,s:'luck',d:0,p:1}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',x:1,fx:1,atk:1,text:'Music hits — {X} is heading to the ring!',ch:[{t:'Get in {X}\'s face',ok:`{A} gets right in {X}'s face. "This isn't your segment." The crowd buzzes.`,g:`{A} meets {X} at the bottom of the ramp and stops nose to nose. "Wrong night. Wrong ring. Wrong person." {X} doesn't move. Neither does {A}.`,no:`{A} steps in front of {X}. "Hey, this is my—" {X} pushes past {A} and takes the mic.`,b:`{A} marches up to {X}. "Back off!" A full step too far away to mean it. {X} pushes past.`,s:'mic',d:.1,hx:12,p:2},{t:'Brawl with {X}',ok:`{A} throws the mic down. "Let's go!" {A} and {X} brawl until referees pour out to separate them.`,g:`{A} drops the mic. "You want it? HERE." Straight at {X}. It spills to the floor, and referees pour out to pull them apart. That's a new rivalry.`,no:`{A} charges. "Come here!" {X} gets the better of the brawl and leaves {A} on the mat.`,b:`{A} charges up the ramp. "You're mine, {X}—" Slips. {X} gets the better of the brawl.`,s:'ring',d:.1,hx:16,p:1},{t:'Leave them to it',ok:`{A} steps back to the corner. "All yours." Watches from the turnbuckle. Cool and unbothered.`,g:`{A} steps back, folds their arms and watches {X} make a mess of it. "Go on. I'll wait." The crowd laughs at {X}.`,no:`{A} shrugs. "Go ahead." {X} takes over the segment. Not a great look.`,b:`{A} waves them off. "Have fun. ...Actually, can I— can I have that back?" {X} won't hand over the mic. Not a great look.`,s:'luck',d:0,hx:4,p:0},{al:'f',t:'Stare {X} down and tell them to wait their turn',ok:`{A} stares {X} down. "Wait your turn." {X} stops halfway down the ramp.`,g:`{A} doesn't move from the center of the ring. Stares {X} down. "You'll get yours. Not tonight. Wait your turn." {X} stops halfway down the ramp.`,no:`{A} stares {X} down. "Wait your turn." {X} keeps walking anyway.`,b:`"Wait your turn!" {X} keeps walking. {A} has to say it again. And again.`,s:'pop',d:.05,hx:8,p:3},{al:'h',t:'Use {X} as a human shield',s:'luck',d:.1,hx:14,p:1,ok:`{A} grabs {X} by the collar. "Sorry, pal." {X} takes the hit meant for {A}. Now {X} is angry too.`,g:`{A} grabs {X}, swings them into the path of the shot, and steps out from behind them. "Thanks, pal." {X} takes the hit. Now {X} is angry too.`,no:`{A} reaches for {X}. "Get over here—" {X} sidesteps, and {A} takes the hit after all.`,b:`{A} grabs {X}. "You're my shield n— wait—" Lets go too early. Both of them take the hit.`}]},
{nhk:'tape',when:'any',fx:1,text:'The mic cuts out mid-sentence.',ch:[{hk:'live',t:'Drop the mic and yell to the crowd',ok:`{A} throws the dead mic aside and cups their hands. "I DON'T NEED IT!" The crowd roars back.`,g:`{A} throws the dead mic aside and screams it with no mic at all: "THIS IS MY HOUSE!" They hear every word and scream it back. Even better than with a mic.`,no:`{A} yells. "You can hear me, right?" Only the front rows can.`,b:`{A} drops the mic. "WHO NEEDS A—" It crackles back on just as {A} trips over the cord.`,s:'pop',d:.1,p:3},{t:'Grab a new mic and keep going',ok:`{A} grabs a new mic. "Where was I? Right." Smooth recovery.`,g:`{A} catches a spare mic from the timekeeper without breaking stride and picks up mid-word. "As I was saying." Smooth.`,no:`{A} taps the new mic. "Hello? Hello?" Also dead. {A} gives up.`,b:`{A} grabs a new mic and forgets where they were. "So... yeah." The moment's gone.`,s:'mic',d:.05,p:2},{hk:'live',al:'h',t:'Scream at the sound tech',s:'mic',d:.05,p:2,ok:`{A} spins toward the sound desk. "You had ONE job!" The poor tech hides under the desk. The fans boo.`,g:`The mic dies mid-word. {A} turns, very slowly, to the sound desk. "I'll wait." The poor tech hides under the desk. The fans boo.`,no:`{A} yells. "Fix it, you useless—" The mic comes back on halfway through. Not a great look.`,b:`{A} rants at the tech. "—and you can tell your boss he's a—" The mic comes back on. The fans boo.`}]},
{nhk:'rally',hk:'live',when:'duo',fx:1,text:'Security floods the ring to separate {A} and {B}.',ch:[{t:'Fight through security',ok:`{A} shoves a guard aside. "Let me at {B}!" Chaos.`,g:`Security piles in. {A} gets through two guards, then a third. "I'm not done!" One more shot on {B} before six of them drag {A} down. Chaos, and the crowd loves it.`,no:`{A} strains against the guards. "Let me GO!" Security holds firm.`,b:`{A} tries to break through. "Out of my— put me DOWN!" Four guards carry {A} out, feet off the ground.`,s:'ring',d:.15,h:12,p:1},{t:'Back off and point at the PPV sign',ok:`{A} backs off and points at the {PPV} sign. "There. That's where it ends."`,g:`{A} stops fighting, steps back and points up at the {PPV} sign. Holds it. Then, quietly: "There." {B} gets the message.`,no:`{A} points. "{PPV}! You hear me?" Security is in the way and nobody sees it.`,b:`{A} points up. "That's where I end you!" It's a sponsor banner. The message gets lost.`,s:'mic',d:.05,h:6,p:2},{al:'h',t:'Hide behind security and taunt {B}',ok:`{A} hides behind a guard and waves. "Come and get me, {B}!" Gutless and infuriating.`,g:`{A} slides behind the wall of guards and waves at {B} through the gap. "Can't reach me? Shame." Gutless and infuriating.`,no:`{A} ducks behind the guards. "Can't touch me!" Security steps aside. {A} is left exposed.`,b:`{A} hides behind the smallest guard. "Ha! Try it!" Security steps aside. {A} is exposed.`,s:'luck',d:0,h:10,p:1}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',w:2,al:'f',atk:1,text:'Something snaps. For a moment, {A} looks at the booing section and smiles…',ch:[{t:'Turn heel! Turn on the crowd and walk out',s:'mic',d:.2,p:4,h:6,turn:true,ok:`"You want to boo me? Fine. I'm done with all of you." {A} walks out. The crowd can't believe it.`,g:`{A} looks at the booing section, smiles, and nods. "You want the bad guy? You've got one." The mic hits the mat. The crowd can't believe it. {A} has a whole new edge.`,no:`{A} glares at the crowd. "You want to boo me? Fine. I'm done with you." Half of them keep cheering. It takes a while to land.`,b:`"I'm done with you people!" {A} walks out through the wrong exit and has to come back past them. It takes a while to land.`},{t:'Shake it off and stay the hero',ok:`{A} takes a breath. "That's not who I am." The fans cheer the restraint.`,g:`{A} looks at the booing section, takes a breath and smiles at them instead. "Not today." And turns back to the fans. The hero stays a hero.`,no:`{A} grits their teeth. "...I'm fine. I'm FINE." It's clear something almost snapped. The crowd is uneasy.`,b:`{A} smiles at the booing section. "No hard feelings." Then glares at them as the camera pans. The crowd is uneasy.`,s:'luck',d:0,p:1}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',w:2,al:'h',atk:1,text:'The fans start cheering {A} anyway. {A} hesitates…',ch:[{t:'Turn face! Embrace the crowd',s:'mic',d:.2,p:4,h:6,turn:true,ok:`{A} lifts the mic, and the cheering just gets louder. "Okay. Okay. I hear you." The building erupts. {A} has come home.`,g:`{A} hears the cheers, closes their eyes and lets them wash over. "I didn't want to need this." A pause. "I need this." The building erupts. {A} has come home.`,no:`{A} raises a hand to the crowd. "Thank you. I, uh, appreciate it." A little stiff. It'll take time, but they're getting there.`,b:`"Okay! I love — I like you. All of you. A lot." It'll take time, but they're getting there.`},{t:'Nobody tells {A} who to be — sneer and leave',ok:`"Nobody tells me who to be." {A} sneers and leaves.`,g:`{A} hears the cheers and sneers. "Nobody tells me who to be. Not them. Not you." And walks out. Cold, defiant, and somehow they cheer harder.`,no:`{A} sneers. "Nobody tells me who to be." Then walks off, looking more confused than defiant.`,b:`"Nobody tells me who — who I am!" {A} walks off. It looks more confused than defiant.`,s:'mic',d:.05,p:1}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',al:'f',text:'A young fan at ringside holds up a homemade {A} sign.',ch:[{t:'Hand the kid their wristband',s:'pop',d:0,p:3,ok:`{A} pulls off the wristband and hands it over. "This is yours now." That kid will remember this forever.`,g:`{A} pulls off the wristband, kneels down at the barricade and puts it on the kid. "Now you have to wear it at my next match. That's the rule." That kid will remember this forever.`,no:`{A} reaches over. "Here, kid—" Security steps in between. It's a quick moment.`,b:`{A} tosses the wristband. "Catch!" It hits the kid's dad. The kid still grabs it.`},{t:'Pose with the sign for the cameras',ok:`{A} holds the kid's sign up for the camera. "This is the best one in here." A lovely moment.`,g:`{A} kneels by the kid and holds the sign up beside their own face for the hard camera. "Best sign in the building." The photo is everywhere by morning.`,no:`{A} grabs the sign. "Get a shot of this!" The camera misses it. The moment is over fast.`,b:`{A} holds up the sign. "Look at this!" Upside down. The kid points it out.`,s:'luck',d:.05,p:4},{t:'Point to the sign and promise a win',ok:`{A} points to the sign. "This one's for you, kid." The crowd loves it.`,g:`{A} points at the sign. "That's my name. In crayon. Somebody believed in it enough to draw it." A beat. "I'm winning this one for you." The kid is losing it.`,no:`{A} points at the sign. "This one's for you, kid!" The kid has already sat down.`,b:`"I'll win for you! For — what's your name?" The kid tells them. {A} gets it wrong.`,s:'mic',d:.1,p:3}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',al:'f',text:'The whole building starts singing {A}\'s entrance music.',ch:[{t:'Sing along',ok:`{A} lowers the mic and joins in. "SING IT!" The whole building sings. A goosebumps moment.`,g:`{A} closes their eyes and sings along with all twenty thousand of them, badly and with total joy. At the end: "I'll never get tired of that." A goosebumps moment.`,no:`{A} sings along. "Whoa-oh—" The crowd is ahead of them by half a verse.`,b:`{A} sings along. "Something something TONIGHT—" Wrong words to their own song. The crowd sings over them.`,s:'pop',d:.05,p:3},{t:'Wait for the peak, then hit the catchphrase',ok:`{A} waits for the peak, then: "AND THAT'S THE BOTTOM LINE!" Big reaction.`,g:`{A} waits. Lets it build. Right at the peak, one line, perfectly timed: "Say it with me." The place comes down.`,no:`{A} jumps in early. "You know what time it—" Lost in the singing.`,b:`{A} waits too long. The singing ends. Silence. "...It's time." A few people clap.`,s:'mic',d:.1,p:4}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',al:'h',text:'A fan in the front row starts heckling {A} — loudly.',ch:[{t:'Get in their face over the barricade',ok:`{A} leans over the barricade. "Say it again. To my face." The heckler backs down.`,g:`{A} walks to the barricade and leans in, close, calm. "Say it again. I'm right here." The heckler sits down. The section laughs at them.`,no:`{A} points at the heckler. "Hey! Sit down!" They keep going, louder. {A} looks petty.`,b:`{A} walks to the barricade. "What'd you say?" The heckler has a better comeback. {A} has nothing. {A} looks petty.`,s:'mic',d:.1,p:2},{t:'Have security throw them out',ok:`{A} snaps at security. "Him. Out." The heckler is walked out. Petty and effective.`,g:`{A} points at the heckler and snaps fingers. Security walks them out. {A} waves the whole way. "Bye!" Petty and perfect.`,no:`{A} points. "Security! Get him out!" Security doesn't move.`,b:`{A} points. "That one! Out!" Security throws out the wrong fan.`,s:'luck',d:0,p:2},{t:'Pour a drink on their sign',ok:`{A} grabs a drink and pours it over the sign. "That's what I think." Huge boos.`,g:`{A} takes a drink from the front row and pours it, slowly, over the heckler's sign. "There. Now it's honest." Huge boos.`,no:`{A} tips the cup. "Here's your sign—" It soaks the fan next to it.`,b:`{A} raises the cup over the sign. "Enjoy this!" It's empty. {A} shakes it at the sign anyway.`,s:'luck',d:.05,p:3}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',al:'h',atk:1,text:'The crowd starts a very rude chant about {A}.',ch:[{t:'Conduct the chant like an orchestra',ok:`{A} raises both hands like a conductor. "And... louder!" The crowd hates how much fun it is.`,g:`{A} raises both hands. "Slower. Louder. Softer. And... cut." The crowd follows every cue without realizing it. The fans hate that it worked.`,no:`{A} waves their arms. "With me now!" The crowd ignores the conducting and keeps chanting.`,b:`{A} conducts. "One, and two, and—" Out of time. It falls apart, and the crowd chants something ruder.`,s:'mic',d:.1,p:3},{t:'Storm off in a huff',ok:`{A} throws down the mic. "I don't need this!" Storms up the ramp. The crowd cheers them out.`,g:`{A} kicks the bottom rope. "You people don't DESERVE me!" Storms up the ramp yelling at every section on the way out. Big, ugly heat.`,no:`{A} storms off. "I'm leaving!" It looks like the crowd won.`,b:`{A} storms off. "Hit my music!" The music doesn't play. {A} storms off in silence.`,s:'luck',d:0,p:1},{t:'Threaten to quit AEW forever',ok:`"Keep chanting and I'll quit AEW forever!" The crowd cheers louder.`,g:`"Fine. I quit. I'm done." {A} drops the mic. Then picks it up. "Unless you apologize." Total heat.`,no:`{A} grips the mic. "One more chant and I quit AEW forever!" The crowd cheers the idea, and {A} has no comeback.`,b:`"I'll quit! Forever! Or — for a while." The crowd cheers the idea.`,s:'mic',d:.15,p:4}]},
{nhk:'rally|attack',hk:'live',when:'duo',al:'h',vs:'f',fx:1,text:'{B} gets the whole crowd chanting against {A}.',ch:[{t:'Blindside {B} mid-chant',ok:`{A} strikes {B} from behind. "Chant THAT." The chant dies instantly.`,g:`{A} waits for {B} to lead the chant, then strikes mid-word. The chant dies instantly. "Keep going, {B}. I'm listening."`,no:`{A} lunges at {B}. "Got y—" {B} sees it coming and steps aside.`,b:`{A} grabs {B}. "Now you're m— wrong arm." {B} steps aside and the chant continues.`,s:'ring',d:.1,h:14,p:1},{t:'Out-talk them',ok:`{A} keeps talking right through it. "...and I'll keep going until you're done." The chant dies. {A} gets the room back.`,g:`{A} doesn't shout over them. Just talks, quietly, until they have to stop to hear. "There. Now. Let me tell you what happens next." {A} wins the room.`,no:`{A} raises their voice. "LISTEN TO ME—" Drowned out.`,b:`{A} tries to out-talk them. "And another — thing — hold on—" Out of breath. The crowd wins.`,s:'mic',d:.15,h:10,p:2}]},
{nhk:'absent|rally',when:'duo',al:'f',vs:'h',fx:1,text:'{B} reaches into their jacket for something…',ch:[{t:'Snatch it before they can use it',ok:`{A} grabs {B}'s wrist. "Looking for this?" Holds up the weapon. Caught.`,g:`{A} grabs {B}'s wrist before it comes out of the jacket and pulls out — brass knuckles. {A} holds them up to the camera. "Cheater." Caught.`,no:`{A} reaches for {B}'s jacket. "Give me th—" {B} gets it out first.`,b:`{A} grabs for the jacket. "Got it!" Wrong pocket. {B} gets it out first.`,s:'ring',d:.1,h:12,p:3},{t:'Call it out so every fan can see',ok:`{A} points at {B}'s jacket. "Ref! Check the pocket!" {B} is caught.`,g:`{A} points straight at the jacket. "Everybody see that? Hand in the pocket? Check it." Every eye turns to {B}. {B} freezes.`,no:`{A} points. "There's a weapon in there!" {B} pulls out a pen. Just a pen. {A} looks foolish.`,b:`{A} points. "That one! Check him!" The wrong person. {B} slips the weapon away.`,s:'mic',d:.05,h:8,p:2}]},
{nhk:'rally|attack',hk:'live',when:'duo',al:'h',vs:'h',fx:1,text:'{A} and {B} both try to leave last — neither will be upstaged.',ch:[{t:'Shove {B} aside and take the spotlight',ok:`{A} shoves {B} aside and takes the center. "My spotlight." Big reaction.`,g:`{A} shoulders {B} aside and takes the center of the ramp, arms up, the last one standing. "That's how you leave a ring." Big reaction.`,no:`{A} shoves {B}. "Move." {B} shoves back. They both just stand there.`,b:`{A} shoves {B} aside. "Step aside for a real—" Trips on the ramp. {B} gets the last pose.`,s:'ring',d:.05,h:10,p:2},{t:'Let {B} go, then trash-talk them behind their back',ok:`{A} waits for {B} to go, then grins. "Did you see the boots? Borrowed." The crowd laughs.`,g:`{A} waves {B} off with a smile. As soon as {B} is through the curtain: "Did you see the boots? They borrowed those." The crowd howls.`,no:`{A} waits, then starts. "So, {B}, between us—" {B} comes back through the curtain halfway through.`,b:`{A} grins. "Now that {B}'s gone—" {B} hasn't left. {B} turns around.`,s:'mic',d:.1,h:8,p:2}]},
{nhk:'rally',hk:'live',when:'duo',al:'f',vs:'f',fx:1,atk:1,text:'The crowd splits down the middle — half for {A}, half for {B}.',ch:[{t:'Play to your half of the crowd',ok:`{A} points at their half. "THIS side gets it!" The split gets louder.`,g:`{A} turns their back on the other side completely. "Only you. Only ever you." Half the building is in love. The other half is furious.`,no:`{A} plays to their half. "Let me hear you!" The other half drowns them out.`,b:`{A} points. "My people!" It's the wrong half. Both halves boo.`,s:'pop',d:.05,h:8,p:3},{t:'Dare {B} to prove who the fans really love',ok:`{A} holds the mic to the crowd. "Who do they love, {B}? Ask them." The crowd answers loudly.`,g:`"You want to know who these people really love, {B}?" {A} holds the mic up to the crowd. "Ask them. Go on. I'll wait." The answer is loud and clear.`,no:`{A} grins. "Let's ask them who they love, {B}!" The crowd answers {B}. Loudly.`,b:`{A} holds out the mic. "Who do you love?" The crowd chants {B}'s name. {A} asks again. Same answer.`,s:'mic',d:.1,h:10,p:2}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',myst:1,w:.3,fx:1,atk:1,text:'The lights go out. When they come back on, a mysterious figure stands on the stage.',ch:[{t:'Challenge the figure',ok:`{A} points at the stage. "Hey! Whoever you are! Come down here!" The figure doesn't move. The crowd is buzzing.`,g:`{A} turns to the stage. "You want to make an entrance? Fine. Next week, come make it in the ring." The figure doesn't move. The crowd is buzzing.`,no:`{A} points at the stage. "You! I see you!" The lights go out again. The figure is gone.`,b:`"Hey! You! Come — come here!" The lights go out. The figure is gone.`,s:'mic',d:.1,p:3},{t:'Pretend it didn\'t happen',ok:`{A} doesn't even turn around. "As I was saying." Cool under pressure.`,g:`{A} doesn't even turn around. "Anyway." And keeps going. Somehow that's scarier than anything.`,no:`{A} keeps going. "So — anyway — " Keeps glancing back at the stage.`,b:`{A} carries on. "Nothing scares me—" The lights flicker. {A} flinches. Everyone sees it.`,s:'luck',d:0,p:1},{t:'Sprint up the ramp after them',ok:`{A} sprints up the ramp. "Get back here!" Gone, but the crowd loves the chase.`,g:`{A} sprints up the ramp, but the figure is gone. {A} stands at the top, scanning the dark, chest heaving. "I'll find you." The crowd loves it.`,no:`{A} reaches the stage. "Where are you?!" Nothing.`,b:`{A} sprints up the ramp. "You can't hide fr—" Runs into a stagehand. The figure is long gone.`,s:'ring',d:.1,p:2}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',atk:1,text:'The commentary team starts arguing about {A} — loud enough for the fans to hear.',ch:[{t:'Grab a headset and set the record straight',ok:`{A} snatches a headset. "Let me correct the record for you." Commentary goes quiet.`,g:`{A} snatches a headset. "I hear you, gentlemen. Let me help. I'm right, you're wrong, and you can go back to the replay." The commentators laugh. So does the crowd.`,no:`{A} grabs a headset. "Excuse me? Say that ag—" It turns into an argument with commentary. Messy.`,b:`{A} grabs a headset. "Now listen here, gentlemen..." It isn't plugged in. {A} talks into it for a while.`,s:'mic',d:.1,p:3},{t:'Ignore it and keep rolling',ok:`{A} never looks over. "Like I was saying." Smooth.`,g:`{A} keeps rolling, never looks over. At the end: "And for the gentlemen at the desk — you're welcome for the material." Smooth.`,no:`{A} pushes on. "At {PPV}, I'm—" The argument at the desk is louder than {A}.`,b:`{A} ignores it. "—and I'm NOT washed up, actually." Answers one of their points by accident.`,s:'luck',d:0,p:1}]},
{hk:'live',when:'any',text:'Pyro goes off early behind {A}.',ch:[{t:'Play it off like it was planned',ok:`{A} doesn't flinch. Turns to the pyro. "Right on cue." The crowd buys it.`,g:`Pyro goes off early. {A} doesn't flinch. Turns, looks at it, nods. "Right on time." The crowd buys it completely.`,no:`{A} jumps, then recovers. "Meant to do that." Everyone saw the jump.`,b:`{A} leaps a foot in the air. "I — that was — planned. Totally." Nobody buys it.`,s:'mic',d:.1,p:3},{t:'Laugh it off with the crowd',ok:`{A} laughs and points at the truck. "Somebody's fired!" Charming.`,g:`{A} laughs, points at the production truck and takes a little bow. "Thank you, I'll be here all week." The crowd laughs with them. Total charm.`,no:`{A} laughs. "Ha. Haha. Okay." A nervous laugh.`,b:`{A} laughs it off. "Didn't scare me at all—" The second round of pyro goes off. {A} hits the deck.`,s:'pop',d:.05,p:2}]},
{hk:'live',when:'solo',text:'The crowd starts chanting for someone else entirely.',ch:[{t:'Remind them who\'s actually standing here',ok:`"Remember who's actually standing here." The crowd comes back around.`,g:`{A} lets the chant run, then: "That's a great name. Chant it at home." A beat. "I'm the one standing here." The crowd turns back.`,no:`{A} points at their own chest. "Hey! I'm the one standing here!" The chant keeps going. {A} has lost them.`,b:`"I'm standing here! Me. Right here." The chant keeps going.`,s:'mic',d:.1,p:2},{t:'Hit a signature move on thin air to win them back',ok:`{A} hits the signature move on thin air and pops up. "That's for whoever's next!" The crowd comes back to them.`,g:`{A} hits the signature move on nothing at all, perfectly, and holds the pose. "Imagine if someone was there." The crowd laughs, then cheers, then chants {A}'s name.`,no:`{A} hits the move on thin air. "...Like that." It looks a little silly. The chant continues.`,b:`{A} goes for the move on thin air. "Watch th— oof." Lands awkwardly. It looks very silly.`,s:'ring',d:.1,p:3},{al:'h',t:'Mock whoever they\'re chanting for',ok:`{A} does a mocking impression of the name they're chanting. "Oh, look at me, everybody loves me." Huge heat.`,g:`{A} mimics the person they're chanting for — the walk, the pose, the voice — then drops it cold. "That's who you want? Really?" Huge heat.`,no:`{A} sneers. "Really? THEM?" The mockery makes the chant louder.`,b:`{A} mocks the name. "Oh, I'm so great, I'm—" The crowd corrects {A}: wrong person. Loudly.`,s:'mic',d:.05,p:2}]}];
const MEV=[
{id:'ref',w:3,text:"A stray elbow catches the referee flush and they crumple in the corner. {A} hits the finisher dead center — and there's nobody to count.",ch:[
 {t:"Send a second referee sprinting down the ramp",s:"luck",st:.25,ok:"The backup ref slides in — one… two… {B} gets a shoulder up! The whole building counts along with the false finish.",g:"The second ref dives in on cue, slapping the mat as the crowd roars every count. One… two… {B} kicks out a hair before three and the place comes apart. \"This is awesome!\" rolls around the arena.",no:"The backup ref is halfway down the ramp when {B} rolls out. The moment's gone before anyone gets there.",b:"The second ref jogs out, gets there late, counts one, and {B} is already sitting up. Commentary has to fill a very long silence."},
 {t:"{X} hits the ring and levels {B} with a steel chair",need:"X",xh:"B",xa:1,s:"luck",d:.05,st:.5,hx:"B",heat:14,ok:"CRACK. {X} drops the chair on {B} and is back over the barricade before the ref stirs. {A} drapes an arm over for the cover.",g:"{X} comes through the crowd, one clean chair shot, and gone — the ref comes to, sees only {A} covering, and counts three. The boos are deafening.",no:"Officials cut {X} off at the bottom of the ramp. A shoving match, but {B} is spared.",b:"{X} slides in, swings, and the chair barely grazes {B}'s shoulder. {X} looks at the chair. The crowd laughs at both of them."},
 {t:"{A} goes low while the ref is down",s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,heat:10,heelA:1,ok:"A low blow nobody official saw. {A} drags {B} to the middle and covers as the ref crawls over.",g:"{A} looks at the ref, looks at the camera, and goes low. Perfectly timed. The ref comes to on cue and slaps the mat three times into a storm of boos.",no:"{B} catches the boot, spins {A} around and fires back. The crowd erupts.",b:"{A} winds up for the low blow, telegraphs it from across the ring, and {B} has to wait for it. You can hear groaning from the cheap seats."},
 {t:"{A} climbs to the top rope to buy time for the ref",s:"ring",d:.15,st:.5,fat:6,ok:"The ref stirs just as {A} comes off the top — a perfect landing and a three count with the ref sliding in. Huge.",g:"{A} perches on the top, waits, waits, the ref's hand twitches — and {A} flies, lands it clean, and the ref crawls in for the three. A finish people will clip all night.",no:"Nobody's there to count it. By the time the ref is up, {B} has rolled to the floor.",b:"{A} climbs, loses footing on the top rope and has to hop down. Then climbs again. The ref is up and watching the whole thing."},
 {t:"{A} revives the referee and keeps it clean",al:"f",s:"pop",d:.05,st:.25,popA:2,ok:"{A} helps the ref up, then wins it the right way. The crowd stands and applauds.",g:"{A} hauls the ref up, dusts them off, points at the mat: \"Count it right.\" Then hits the finisher again and the ref counts three. The arena loves them for it.",no:"By the time the ref is on their feet, {B} has recovered and the moment is gone.",b:"{A} spends so long fanning the ref with a towel that {B} gets up, walks over and rolls {A} up for two. The crowd groans."},
 {t:"{A} grabs a handful of tights on a roll-up as the ref comes to",al:"h",s:"luck",d:.05,st:.25,heat:12,ok:"One… two… three! A handful of tights steals it. Instant boos.",g:"The ref comes to, sees a cradle, counts — and the camera zooms in on {A}'s fist full of tights. Three. The crowd tears into the ref, and {A} sprints up the ramp grinning.",no:"The ref spots the hand and waves the count off. The crowd cheers the ref.",b:"{A} grabs so much tights it pulls {B} half out of the cover. Even the ref has to stop and stare."},
 {t:"{A} peels the pad off the top turnbuckle while the ref is out",al:"h",vs:"f",s:"luck",d:.05,st:.25,heat:10,ok:"Exposed steel. {B} gets whipped face-first into it and crumples. The boos are thunderous.",g:"{A} unhooks the pad and tosses it to the floor with a smirk to the hard camera. Irish whip, steel, three. Every fan in the building is on their feet shouting at the ref.",no:"{B} reverses the whip and {A} eats the exposed steel instead. The crowd erupts.",b:"{A} can't get the pad's knot undone and fumbles with it for an age. The ref sits up and watches them do it."}]},
{id:'chair',w:3,bd:1,text:"{B} slides a steel chair into the ring and the crowd starts buzzing.",ch:[
 {t:"{A} boots the chair away and hits the finisher",s:"ring",d:.05,st:.25,popA:2,ok:"{A} kicks the chair back out to the floor and plants {B} right where they stand. Three. Poetic justice.",g:"{B} swings, {A} ducks, boots the chair into the front row and nails the finisher in one motion. The crowd erupts before the ref hits two.",no:"The chair skids under {A}'s feet. The finish gets tangled and nobody quite pops.",b:"{A} kicks at the chair, misses it, then trips over it on the way to the finisher. Commentary goes very quiet."},
 {t:"{A} swings the chair behind the referee's back",loseNo:"dq",s:"luck",d:.1,st:.5,heat:10,heelA:1,ok:"The ref turns away. CRACK. {A} covers and 10,000 people scream at the ref.",g:"{A} waits for the ref to check on the rope, steps in, one perfect chair shot and tosses it out before the ref turns. Three. The crowd is apoplectic.",no:"The ref turns back right as the chair comes down. Disqualification.",b:"{A} winds up so slowly the ref turns back, sees everything, and calls for the bell."},
 {t:"The ref catches it all — throw the match out",rematch:1,dq:1,always:1,st:-.25,heat:18,nc:1,ok:"The ref signals for the bell: no contest! Both wrestlers keep swinging after the bell. This feud just went nuclear.",g:"The ref waves it off, and neither of them cares — they brawl straight through security and up the ramp. Fans are on their feet chanting for a rematch."},
 {t:"They fight over the chair until it flies out of the ring",s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,fat:5,heat:8,ok:"A tug-of-war that sends the chair sailing over the top rope — and {A} comes out of it on top.",g:"Push, pull, a headbutt to break it, and the chair goes spinning into the timekeeper's area. {A} catches {B} on the rebound with a clothesline that flips them inside out.",no:"The tug-of-war looks clumsy and ends with nobody really winning.",b:"They both let go at once and the chair clatters harmlessly to the mat. They stare at it. So does the crowd."},
 {t:"{A} tosses the chair out and dares {B} to fight fair",al:"f",s:"pop",d:.05,st:.25,popA:2,heat:6,ok:"\"Come on, then!\" {A} flings the chair aside and the fans roar for a straight fight.",g:"{A} folds the chair, hands it to the timekeeper, turns to {B} and beckons with both hands. The arena goes wild — and {A} beats {B} with fists alone.",no:"{B} uses the moment to catch {A} with a cheap shot.",b:"{A} throws the chair out of the ring, but it bounces off the apron right back in. {B} picks it up."},
 {t:"{A} stashes the chair under the ring for later",al:"h",stash:1,s:"luck",d:0,st:.25,heat:8,ok:"Smart and sneaky. The chair goes under the apron. It'll be there when {A} needs it.",g:"{A} slides the chair under the ring and gives the hard camera a wink. Commentary can't believe it. That chair is coming back some night.",no:"The camera catches it, and the front row points it out to the ref.",b:"{A} tries to slide the chair under the ring but it's too tall and sticks out. The ref pulls it right back out."},
 {t:"The ref confiscates it and {B} throws a tantrum",al:"h",vs:"h",always:1,st:.25,heat:6,ok:"{B} melts down at the ref, and {A} capitalizes with a cheap shot from behind.",g:"{B} screams in the ref's face about a \"conspiracy\" — and {A} rolls them up from behind with a fistful of tights. Two heels outplaying each other. The crowd loves to hate it."}]},
{id:'hurt',w:1.5,text:"{B} lands awkwardly on the outside and grabs a knee. The ref leans in — and then crosses their arms in an X.",ch:[
 {t:"Call an audible and take it home now",iB:.2,always:1,st:-.5,ok:"A fast, simple finish. {B} limps to the back under their own power. The crowd applauds the effort.",g:"The ref whispers, the finish changes on the fly, and it's over in thirty seconds without anyone noticing. Seamless. {B} gets a standing ovation on the way out."},
 {t:"Let {B} push through",iB:.15,s:"luck",d:.25,st:.5,popB:3,failInj:"B",ok:"{B} waves off the trainer and fights on. A gutsy, heroic performance. The fans give them a standing ovation.",g:"{B} limps, grits, and still hits everything — and the crowd chants {B}'s name all the way to the finish. \"You deserve it!\" A warrior's performance.",no:"{B} can't continue. The ref stops it and the trainers come out. It looks serious.",b:"{B} tries one more move, the leg gives out, and the ref waves it off. The crowd goes deathly quiet."},
 {t:"Have the doctor check {B} at ringside while {A} waits",iB:.25,always:1,st:0,ok:"The doctor clears {B}, and they finish strong. A scare, nothing more.",g:"The doctor checks the knee, {B} nods, and the crowd starts a slow clap that builds into a roar. {B} comes back in fired up and the closing stretch is better for the pause."},
 {t:"{A} checks on {B} before finishing the match",al:"f",iB:.3,always:1,st:.25,popA:2,ok:"{A} kneels by {B}, checks they're okay, then finishes it. A classy moment the fans won't forget.",g:"{A} waves off the ref, crouches next to {B} and taps their chest — \"You good?\" — then helps them up before the finish. The crowd applauds both of them."},
 {t:"{A} goes straight for the bad knee",al:"h",iB:.6,iBn:.3,s:"ring",d:.05,st:.25,heat:15,ok:"Cruel and calculated. {A} wrenches the knee until {B} taps.",g:"{A} stomps the knee, wraps it around the ring post and locks in a leg submission. {B} taps in seconds. The boos are some of the loudest of the night.",no:"{B} fires up out of pure spite and drives {A} away with a flurry.",b:"{A} grabs the wrong leg. {B} has to quietly switch legs mid-hold. Commentary pretends not to notice."}]},
{id:'dead',w:2,text:"A long rest hold, and the crowd is sitting on its hands. Somebody up top yells \"Boring!\"",ch:[
 {t:"Go to a big spot off the top rope",ntrait:'monster|suplex',s:"ring",d:.2,st:.5,fat:8,ok:"Off the top and dead-on. The building wakes right up.",g:"{A} scales the turnbuckles, the crowd stands, and the dive lands with a slap you can hear on the broadcast. Instantly loud again.",no:"{A} overshoots it and crashes. The crowd winces.",b:"{A} slips on the second rope, lands on the turnbuckle sideways, and does the move anyway — badly. A sing-song chant lets them know exactly what everyone saw."},
 {t:"Play to the crowd with a comedy spot",s:"mic",d:.1,st:.25,popA:1,ok:"A bit of comedy gets the crowd laughing, and they're back into the match.",g:"{A} sits {B} in the corner like a naughty kid, conducts the crowd like an orchestra, and leads them in a call-and-response. Laughter, then a roar. A dead crowd, resurrected.",no:"The joke lands with a thud. Somebody coughs.",b:"{A} tries a comedy spot nobody understands. {B} doesn't either. They both just stand there for a second."},
 {t:"Stay the course and let it breathe",always:1,st:0,ok:"It picks back up, eventually.",g:"{A} works the hold with purpose, and when {B} finally fights out, the crowd is all the way back."},
 {t:"Trade hard chops in the middle of the ring",s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,fat:5,heat:6,ok:"Chop! Chop! Chop! The crowd \"WOOOs\" along with every one.",g:"Open-hand chops that echo off the roof. Chests turn purple. Every chop gets a louder \"WOOO\" until the crowd is begging for more.",no:"The chops look soft and the \"WOOO\"s die out.",b:"The chops land on the shoulder, the neck, the air. One falls short entirely. The crowd stops woo-ing."},
 {t:"Get the crowd clapping to rally {A}",al:"f",s:"pop",d:.05,st:.5,popA:1,ok:"The clapping builds and {A} fights up to their feet. The building is back.",g:"One clap, then another, then the whole arena clapping in rhythm. {A} feeds off every beat and powers out. Goosebumps.",no:"Only a handful of fans join in.",b:"{A} starts the clap and nobody follows it. {A} claps alone for a bit, then gives up."},
 {t:"{A} mocks the crowd for being so quiet",al:"h",s:"mic",d:.1,st:.25,popA:1,ok:"\"Is this a library?\" Now they're loud — and furious.",g:"{A} cups an ear, mimes snoring, and tells the crowd they're the worst in the country. Thunderous boos. {A} smiles and goes back to work.",no:"They stay quiet. That's worse.",b:"{A} grabs at the crowd with an insult that just isn't funny. A handful of people boo politely."}]},
{id:'runin',w:3,need:"X",text:"{X}'s music hits in the middle of the match and the whole arena turns to the stage!",ch:[
 {t:"{X} goes after {B}",xh:"B",s:"luck",st:.25,hx:"B",heat:15,ok:"{X} hits the ring and lays out {B}. The crowd erupts.",g:"The lights flash, {X} marches down with a purpose, and a single shot puts {B} on the mat. {X} leaves before the ref can react. The roof nearly comes off.",no:"{B} sees it coming and fights {X} off. Security drags {X} up the ramp.",b:"{X} runs down, slides in, and slips on the apron. By the time they're up, {B} is waiting."},
 {t:"Swerve! {X} costs {A} the match",xh:"A",always:1,st:.25,flip:1,hx:"A",heat:18,ok:"{X} pulls the distraction — and {B} steals the win. {A} is livid. {X} is smiling.",g:"The crowd thinks {X} is there to help. Then {X} trips {A} off the top rope and walks away clapping. {B} rolls {A} up. Three. The boos are mixed with gasps."},
 {t:"Security cuts {X} off at the top of the ramp",always:1,st:0,hx:"A",heat:6,ok:"Security swarms {X} at the stage. The seed is planted for another day.",g:"A wall of security holds {X} back while {A} stares up the ramp. The two lock eyes. Next week's main event just booked itself."},
 {t:"{A} wipes out {X} with a dive to the floor",al:"f",xal:"h",crowd:'flip|chaos|tech',s:"ring",d:.15,st:.5,hx:"A",heat:10,popA:2,fat:5,ok:"{A} flies over the top rope onto {X}, then rolls {B} up for three. Huge pop!",g:"{A} sprints the ropes, flies over the top and wipes out {X} at the bottom of the ramp, rolls back in and hits the finisher on {B}. One of the loudest pops of the night.",no:"{A} dives and crashes into the barricade. {X} walks away untouched.",b:"{A} goes for the dive, clips the top rope, and lands on the apron. {X} stops and looks at them."},
 {t:"{X} holds {B} while {A} hits the finisher",al:"h",xal:"h",s:"luck",d:.05,st:.25,hx:"B",heat:16,ok:"Two-on-one and a cheap three. The boos are deafening.",g:"{X} holds {B}'s arms behind their back, {A} slaps them across the face, and then the finisher. The ref somehow saw none of it. Garbage is flying into the ring.",no:"{B} escapes at the last second and {A} flattens {X} by mistake.",b:"{X} holds {B} so loosely that {B} just walks out of it. {A} has to stop mid-run."}]},
{id:'finish',w:3,big:1,text:"Near-fall after near-fall. The whole building is on its feet, chanting \"This is awesome!\" How does it end?",ch:[
 {t:"One more false finish",s:"ring",d:.15,st:.75,fat:6,ok:"Kickout at two-point-nine! Then the finish. The crowd is hoarse.",g:"Finisher. Kickout. The arena gasps. Then another — and the ref's hand hangs in the air as {B} gets a toe on the rope. Then the finish, for real. People are hugging strangers.",no:"They go to the well once too often and the crowd deflates.",b:"They go for the false finish, but {B}'s kickout is a beat late and the ref has to fake a slow count. Everyone saw it."},
 {t:"{A} hits the finisher clean",always:1,st:.25,popA:2,ok:"1… 2… 3. Decisive.",g:"No tricks, no swerves — {A} hits it perfectly and the crowd counts along. A clean win that means something."},
 {t:"Swerve! {B} steals a roll-up",always:1,st:.25,flip:1,heat:12,ok:"{B} steals it with a roll-up! Nobody saw that coming.",g:"{A} goes for the finisher, {B} slides out the back and wraps them up in a crucifix. Three. The crowd gasps, then explodes."},
 {t:"They trade finishers until one stays down",s:"ring",d:.2,st:.75,fat:8,ok:"Finisher for finisher. Kickout. Kickout. Then one stays down. An all-time finishing stretch.",g:"They trade every move in their arsenals — and each kickout is louder than the last. When one finally stays down, the fans stand and chant \"Fight forever!\"",no:"They run out of gas and the last few moves get sloppy.",b:"They go for one finisher too many and it falls apart: the timing slips, a reversal is missed, and the cover is ugly. The crowd boos the finish."},
 {t:"{A} fires up for a comeback flurry",al:"f",s:"pop",d:.1,st:.75,popA:3,ok:"Hope spot, comeback, finisher — the crowd loses its mind.",g:"{A} shakes off a big shot, punches back, then hits everything in the arsenal. Each move gets louder. The finisher gets the loudest pop of the night.",no:"The comeback gets cut off too many times and the crowd stops believing.",b:"{A} fires up and runs straight into a clothesline, then fires up again and runs into the same clothesline. The crowd stops cheering."},
 {t:"{A} puts their feet on the ropes for leverage",al:"h",s:"luck",d:.05,st:.25,heat:14,ok:"Feet on the ropes, three count. The fans are screaming at the ref.",g:"{A} drapes both boots on the middle rope, the ref counts three on the wrong side, and {A} slides out before the replay hits the screen. The ref is booed for five straight minutes.",no:"The ref spots the feet and stops the count.",b:"{A} reaches for the ropes with one foot, misses, then props the other foot up — on the side the ref is facing. The ref sees all of it."},
 {t:"{B} tries a cheap roll-up — {A} reverses it",vs:"h",s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,popA:2,heat:10,ok:"{A} rolls through the roll-up and holds the tights this time. Hoisted by their own petard!",g:"{B} tries to steal it, {A} reads it, reverses, and holds on. Three. The crowd laughs in {B}'s face.",no:"The reversal is botched and both end up in a tangle.",b:"The reversal gets twisted up so badly the ref doesn't know whose shoulders are down. Nor does anyone else."}]},
{id:'floor',w:2,text:"The action spills over the barricade and into the crowd. Fans scatter.",ch:[
 {t:"Brawl up into the stands",s:"ring",d:.15,st:.5,fat:8,ok:"Fans scatter as they trade shots between the seats.",g:"Up the stairs, through the rows, trading punches on the concourse while phones light up the arena. The camera follows every step. Chaos — the good kind.",no:"It's hard to see anything on camera and the crowd at home is lost.",b:"They brawl into the crowd and immediately get stuck behind a row of chairs. The camera shows them waiting for fans to move."},
 {t:"Double count-out",rematch:1,dq:1,always:1,st:-.25,heat:20,nc:1,ok:"Neither makes it back. The bell rings — and they're still fighting. This isn't over.",g:"The ref counts ten, the bell rings, and they keep swinging all the way to the back. Every fan in the building wants the rematch."},
 {t:"Get it back in the ring",always:1,st:0,ok:"Back to business.",g:"{A} tosses {B} back in with a glance at the ref. The match never loses a beat."},
 {t:"Fight all the way up the entrance ramp",s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,fat:6,heat:8,ok:"They brawl to the stage and back. The crowd follows every step.",g:"They fight up the ramp, off the stage set and back down, and the crowd is standing the whole way. A spectacle.",no:"It drags on too long and the ref has to count them back.",b:"The brawl stalls at the top of the ramp while they figure out what to do next. A long walk back to the ring."},
 {t:"{A} dives off the top rope onto {B} on the floor",al:"f",crowd:'flip|chaos|tech',iAn:.5,s:"ring",d:.15,st:.5,fat:6,popA:2,ok:"\"THIS IS AWESOME!\" chants fill the arena.",g:"{A} sprints across the ring, springs off the top rope and wipes out {B} on the floor. The barricade buckles. The front row is on its feet, shrieking.",no:"{B} moves and {A} crashes hard on the floor.",b:"{A} goes for the dive, clips their foot on the top rope and lands on the apron instead. It looks painful. The crowd groans."},
 {t:"{A} rams {B} into the steel steps",al:"h",iB:.15,s:"ring",d:.05,st:.25,heat:12,ok:"A sickening thud. {A} smirks.",g:"{A} lines up {B}, takes a run and drives them shoulder-first into the steel steps. The steps come apart. The crowd gasps, then boos.",no:"{B} blocks it and {A} goes into the steps instead.",b:"{A} pushes {B} at the steps, but they miss by a foot. {B} has to throw themselves into them."}]},
{id:'miscomm',w:3,need:"A2",text:"{A2} swings at {B} — {B} ducks — and {A2} nails their own partner {A}!",ch:[
 {t:"They shake it off and win together",s:"luck",st:.25,chemT:1,ok:"A quick apology, a double-team finisher, and crisis averted.",g:"{A2} holds up both hands — \"My bad!\" — {A} nods, and they hit their double-team finisher in perfect sync. The crowd cheers the save.",no:"The tension lingers all the way to the finish, and it shows.",b:"They try to hug it out and bump heads. The crowd laughs at them."},
 {t:"Tease a breakup",split:1,s:"mic",d:.05,st:.5,heatT:15,chemT:-2,ok:"{A} shoves {A2} after the bell. Trouble in paradise…",g:"{A} stares at {A2} on the ramp, then turns and walks away. {A2} calls after them. The crowd gasps. This team is in real trouble.",no:"The tease is so subtle nobody notices.",b:"{A} shoves {A2} so softly it looks like a pat. Even commentary can't sell it."},
 {t:"{A} and {A2} hug it out in the middle of the ring",al:"f",s:"pop",d:0,st:.25,chemT:2,ok:"The crowd cheers the reunion. They're closer than ever.",g:"{A} grabs {A2} by the back of the head, forehead to forehead, then a hug. The fans stand and applaud. This team just got stronger.",no:"The hug is awkward. Very awkward.",b:"They go in for the hug, it turns into a handshake, then a high-five. The crowd is confused."},
 {t:"{A} slaps {A2} and demands they get it together",al:"h",s:"mic",d:.1,st:.25,heatT:10,chemT:-1,ok:"Harsh, but it works — for now.",g:"{A} slaps {A2} across the face, screams \"FOCUS!\" and they go out and win. The crowd boos and cheers at the same time.",no:"{A2} glares back. This isn't over.",b:"{A} winds up and misses the slap. {A2} just stares at them."}]},
{id:'invade',w:4,fd:1,need:"Y",text:"{Y} from {RIVAL} hops the barricade and storms the ring!",ch:[
 {t:"Everyone fights {Y} off",fdx:"A",s:"ring",d:.05,st:.25,hy:"A",heat:15,ok:"{Y} is sent packing. The brand war is on.",g:"{A} and {B} stop fighting each other long enough to clothesline {Y} over the top. The crowd chants the brand's name. War.",no:"{Y} escapes after landing a few shots.",b:"They all go for {Y} at once and collide with each other. {Y} laughs and leaves."},
 {t:"{Y} lays out {A} and poses",fdx:"A",yh:"A",always:1,st:.25,hy:"A",heat:22,popA:-1,ok:"{Y} stands tall over {A}. War has been declared.",g:"{Y} drops {A} with one shot and holds the rival brand's colors over the body. The boos are tinged with genuine shock."},
 {t:"Ignore it and finish the match",always:1,st:0,ok:"Security handles it. The match goes on.",g:"Security bundles {Y} out, and {A} and {B} pick up exactly where they left off. Pros."},
 {t:"{A} dives through the ropes onto {Y}",al:"f",crowd:'flip|chaos|tech',fdx:"A",iAn:.5,s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,hy:"A",heat:14,popA:2,ok:"{A} defends the brand! Huge pop.",g:"{A} spots {Y}, sprints, and flies through the ropes like a missile. {Y} is down, and the crowd sings {A}'s name.",no:"{Y} catches {A} and throws them into the barricade.",b:"{A} dives, {Y} steps aside, and {A} goes into the barricade. {Y} walks off with a wave."},
 {t:"{A} hides behind the ref and lets {Y} deal with {B}",al:"h",yh:"B",fdx:"B",fdxNo:"A",s:"luck",d:0,st:.25,hy:"B",heat:14,ok:"{Y} takes out {B}, and {A} strolls over for the pin.",g:"{A} ducks behind the ref, {Y} levels {B}, and {A} calmly covers for three. Opportunism at its finest. The crowd is furious.",no:"{Y} goes after {A} instead.",b:"{A} hides so badly behind the ref that {Y} walks right past {B} to {A}."}]},
{id:'belt',w:3,vs:"h",title:1,text:"While the ref checks on a fallen wrestler, {B} slides the {T} title belt into the ring.",ch:[
 {t:"Belt shot! {B} steals the win",always:1,flip:1,st:.25,heat:18,ok:"{B} cracks {A} with the gold and steals it!",g:"{B} winds up, the gold catches the light, CRACK. {A} is out cold. The ref turns back to see a cover. Three. Garbage hits the ring."},
 {t:"The ref snatches the belt away",s:"luck",st:.25,heat:8,ok:"Order is restored — for now.",g:"The ref rips the belt from {B}'s hands and tosses it to ringside. The crowd cheers. {B} pleads innocence.",no:"The ref fumbles the belt and the moment gets confusing.",b:"The ref drops the belt on their own foot. Everyone stops."},
 {t:"{A} ducks the belt shot and hits the finisher",s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,popA:2,ok:"The belt goes flying and {A} gets the win.",g:"{B} swings, {A} ducks, the belt sails out, and the finisher lands before {B} can turn around. The crowd roars.",no:"The ducking spot looks rehearsed.",b:"{A} ducks before {B} even swings. {B} has to swing anyway. Commentary goes quiet."},
 {t:"{A} wrestles the belt away and hands it to the ref",al:"f",s:"ring",d:.05,st:.25,popA:2,heat:8,ok:"Doing it the right way — and winning anyway.",g:"{A} rips the belt away, hands it to the ref with a nod, and beats {B} clean. The crowd chants {A}'s name.",no:"The handoff gives {B} time to recover.",b:"{A} hands the ref the belt, the ref drops it, {A} picks it up again. {B} attacks."},
 {t:"{A} grabs the belt first and nails {B} with it",al:"h",loseNo:"dq",s:"luck",d:.1,st:.5,heat:14,ok:"{A} wins with the belt they were fighting for. Dastardly.",g:"{A} snatches the gold and swings without hesitating. {B} drops. {A} poses with the belt they just used as a weapon. The crowd is livid.",no:"The ref turns around and catches everything. Disqualification.",b:"{A} swings and misses so badly the belt flies into the crowd. A fan catches it."}]},
{id:'rally',w:2,al:"f",text:"The whole building is stomping the bleachers and chanting {A}'s name. {B} looks around, rattled.",ch:[
 {t:"Feed off the crowd and fire up",s:"pop",d:.05,st:.5,popA:2,ok:"{A} pops up on every beat of the chant, shrugs off {B}'s shots and starts firing back. The place is shaking.",g:"{A} stops selling. Stands up straight in the middle of the ring while {B} punches, nodding along to the chant. Then one forearm, two, three, and {B} is reeling. The comeback is pure electricity.",no:"{B} cuts the comeback off with a thumb to the eye. The chant stalls.",b:"{A} fires up a beat too early, runs the ropes and straight into {B}'s boot. The chant fizzles out mid-word."},
 {t:"Hit a signature move to pop the crowd",s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,ok:"The signature lands right at the peak of the chant. The place comes unglued.",g:"{A} waits — lets the chant swell one more time — then hits the signature so crisply the sound of it carries to the back row. People are standing on their seats.",no:"The move is slightly off, and the pop is a little muted.",b:"{A} calls for the signature, {B} isn't in position, and it lands half on, half off. The chant dies in the middle. A few people laugh."},
 {t:"Stay composed and wrestle smart",always:1,st:.25,ok:"{A} soaks it in but doesn't get carried away. Calm, efficient, effective.",g:"{A} lets the crowd do the work, picks the moment and wins with a simple move done perfectly. The veterans in the back will love that one."},
 {t:"Climb and fly off the top rope for the crowd",s:"ring",d:.2,st:.75,fat:6,popA:1,ok:"{A} climbs, the crowd counts \"three… two… one…\" and the splash lands flush. An unforgettable moment.",g:"The whole building counts down. {A} stands tall on the top rope, arms out, and flies — a picture-perfect splash and the loudest pop of the night. Phones are up in every row.",no:"{B} gets the knees up at the last second.",b:"{A} takes off from the top before {B} is in place and lands flat on the canvas. The countdown chant turns into a long, low \"ohhhh\"."}]},
{id:'cheat',w:2,al:"h",text:"The ref is busy with a commotion on the apron, back turned to the ring. {A} sees their chance.",ch:[
 {t:"Rake {B}'s eyes",s:"luck",d:0,st:.25,heat:10,ok:"A quick rake, a roll-up, and the ref turns back just in time to count. Dirty and effective.",g:"{A} rakes the eyes, cradles {B} and hooks the leg in one motion — the ref turns round to a pinfall already set. Three. The crowd is apoplectic.",no:"The ref turns back just in time. Busted.",b:"{A} goes for the eyes and catches {B}'s forehead. {B} just looks at them. So does the ref."},
 {t:"Slip on the brass knuckles",loseNo:"dq",s:"luck",d:.1,st:.5,heat:14,ok:"One punch with the knuckles and {B} is out. Lights out.",g:"{A} slides the knuckles out of the trunks, one punch, and they're back in hiding before the ref turns. {B} is out cold. The boos are mixed with debris hitting the ring.",no:"The knuckles clatter to the mat and the ref sees everything. Disqualification.",b:"{A} fumbles the knuckles, drops them on the mat, and has to bend down and pick them up in front of the ref."},
 {t:"Use the ropes for leverage on a pin",s:"ring",d:.05,st:.25,heat:10,ok:"Feet on the ropes. 1… 2… 3. Nobody official saw it. Everybody else did.",g:"{A} drapes a foot over the middle rope, the ref counts three on the far side, and the replay plays in slow motion on the big screen. The boos are thunderous.",no:"The ref kicks the foot off the rope and the cover is broken.",b:"{A} reaches for the rope and misses by a foot, then scoots over to try again. The ref is watching all of it."},
 {t:"Spit a mist of water in {B}'s face",s:"luck",d:.05,st:.25,heat:12,ok:"Water right in the eyes. Disgusting. The crowd is outraged.",g:"{A} takes a mouthful, waits for {B} to turn, and sprays it right into their eyes. Roll-up. Three. The front row is screaming at the ref.",no:"{B} ducks and the ref gets drenched.",b:"{A} spits, and most of it dribbles down {A}'s own chin. Even the crowd laughs."}]},
{id:'boos',w:1.5,al:"h",text:"\"{A} sucks! {A} sucks!\" The chant is coming from every corner of the building.",ch:[
 {t:"Stop mid-match to argue with a fan",s:"mic",d:.1,st:.25,popA:1,ok:"{A} leans over the ropes to scream at a fan. The crowd hates it — which means it works.",g:"{A} spots the loudest fan in the front row, gets in their face across the barricade, then turns to the camera mocking them. The whole section is on its feet booing.",no:"{B} capitalizes on the distraction and takes over.",b:"{A} picks an argument with a fan who just shrugs and waves. {B} gets up and hits {A} from behind."},
 {t:"Take it out on {B}",s:"ring",d:.05,st:.5,heat:10,ok:"{A} turns every boo into another stomp on {B}. Cold and calculated.",g:"{A} stops, listens to the chant, smiles — and goes to work on {B} with such contempt that the boos turn into a roar of hatred.",no:"{A} gets sloppy in their anger.",b:"{A} gets so worked up they forget the match, and walk right into {B}'s best move."},
 {t:"Conduct the chant from the top rope",s:"mic",d:.15,st:.5,popA:1,ok:"{A} stands on the turnbuckle waving their arms like a conductor. The boos double.",g:"{A} climbs to the top and conducts the chant — \"Louder! I can't hear you!\" — then dives on {B} at the peak. A heel masterpiece.",no:"{B} knocks them off the top.",b:"{A} loses balance on the turnbuckle and has to hop down. The chant gets louder, aimed at the hop."}]},
{id:'hope',w:2,vs:"f",text:"{B} is fighting from underneath. The crowd is stomping, clapping, begging for a comeback.",ch:[
 {t:"{A} cuts the comeback off cold",s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,heat:10,ok:"{B} gets to their feet, the crowd surges — and {A} drops them with one shot. Silence.",g:"{B} rises, the crowd rises with them, three punches, four — and {A} snaps them down with one perfect cut-off. You can hear a single fan say \"no\". Masterful.",no:"{A} mistimes it and {B} builds momentum.",b:"{A} goes for the cut-off, {B} isn't there, and {A} stumbles into the corner. The crowd cheers the mistake."},
 {t:"Let {B} make the big comeback before {A} wins",s:"ring",d:.15,st:.75,popB:2,fat:5,ok:"{B}'s comeback has the building on its feet. Then {A} turns it around. A rollercoaster finish where even the loser wins.",g:"{B} fires up, hits everything, gets a near-fall that has strangers grabbing each other — and {A} catches them in mid-air. Three. Both get a standing ovation.",no:"The comeback is short-lived.",b:"{B}'s comeback runs out of steam after two moves. The crowd sits back down."},
 {t:"Swerve! {B} completes the comeback and wins",always:1,st:.5,flip:1,popB:3,ok:"The fairy tale comes true! The crowd erupts.",g:"{B} fights back, hits everything, gets the three. The building shakes. Strangers are hugging in the stands."}]},
{id:'stall',w:1.5,vs:"h",text:"{B} is in the ref's face, arguing about a slow count — buying time while the crowd chants \"Boring!\"",ch:[
 {t:"{A} waits, then strikes",s:"ring",d:.05,st:.25,ok:"{A} leans on the ropes, arms folded, until {B} turns around — then levels them.",g:"{A} sits on the second rope, checks their wrist like a watch, and the crowd laughs. When {B} finally turns around, {A} drops them with one shot. Roar.",no:"{B} buys enough time to recover.",b:"{A} waits so long that {B} fully recovers and walks straight back into control."},
 {t:"{A} rolls {B} up while they're distracted",s:"luck",d:.05,st:.25,popA:2,heat:8,ok:"{B} is mid-sentence with the ref when {A} cradles them. 1… 2… 3!",g:"{B} is still jawing at the ref when {A} slides in behind, folds them up in a schoolboy and the ref has no choice but to count. Three. The crowd laughs in {B}'s face.",no:"{B} kicks out in shock.",b:"{A} goes for the roll-up, tangles their own legs, and they both sort of fall over. The ref doesn't count anything."},
 {t:"{A} joins in yelling at the ref",al:"h",s:"mic",d:.1,st:.25,heat:6,ok:"Two heels berating a ref at once. The crowd is fuming.",g:"{A} and {B} take turns jabbing the ref in the chest and the ref backs into a corner. The fans are booing so loudly the commentators have to shout.",no:"The ref threatens {A} with a disqualification and they back right off.",b:"{A} starts yelling, loses track of what they're mad about, and trails off. The ref just waits."},
 {t:"{A} gets the crowd to count {B} down",al:"f",s:"pop",d:.05,st:.5,popA:1,ok:"\"FIVE! FOUR! THREE!\" {B} panics and scrambles back into the action.",g:"{A} raises an arm and the whole building counts along. {B} panics, rushes back — straight into {A}'s finisher. Three. The crowd takes all the credit.",no:"The count fizzles out after three.",b:"{A} starts the count and almost nobody follows. {A} counts alone for a while, then stops."}]},
{id:'respect',w:1.5,al:"f",vs:"f",text:"Two fan favorites, battered and exhausted, and the crowd is on its feet applauding: \"This is awesome! This is awesome!\"",ch:[
 {t:"Trade strikes from their knees up to their feet",s:"ring",d:.1,st:.5,fat:5,ok:"From their knees to their feet, strike for strike. The crowd yells with every one.",g:"Knees, then one knee, then standing, forearm for forearm, every shot louder than the last. The arena stands and chants \"Fight forever!\"",no:"They're too exhausted to sell it.",b:"The strikes are so soft they look like pats on the arm. The applause drains away."},
 {t:"Shake hands mid-match, then go at it again",s:"pop",d:.05,st:.5,popA:1,popB:1,ok:"Respect — and then war. Beautiful.",g:"They grab hands, hold it a second, nod — and {A} snaps a kick to {B}'s head. Respect, then war. The crowd applauds the handshake and roars the kick.",no:"The handshake kills the momentum.",b:"They go to shake and miss each other's hand entirely. They try again. The crowd is unsure what's happening."},
 {t:"{A} ends it with a flash pin",always:1,st:.25,ok:"A quick finish between two equals.",g:"{A} catches {B} in a small package out of nowhere. Three. {B} sits up, laughs, and nods. They both get a standing ovation."}]},
{id:'villains',w:1.5,al:"h",vs:"h",text:"Two villains, and neither will stop cheating. The ref has completely lost control.",ch:[
 {t:"Both go for low blows at the same time",s:"luck",d:0,st:.5,heat:12,ok:"A double low blow! They both collapse. The crowd howls with laughter.",g:"They look at each other, look at the ref, and both swing low at the same moment. Down they go. The crowd is laughing too hard to boo.",no:"They both block. Nobody's sure what to do next.",b:"They both swing, both miss, and catch each other in the thigh. Neither sells it."},
 {t:"{A} out-cheats {B} with something from their boot",s:"luck",d:.1,st:.5,heat:14,ok:"The better cheater wins.",g:"{B} goes for the knuckles; {A} already has a roll of quarters in the fist. Three. Even the crowd is a little impressed.",no:"{B} out-cheats them right back.",b:"{A} reaches into the boot and comes up with nothing. {B} reaches into theirs and doesn't."},
 {t:"Double DQ — the ref has had enough",rematch:1,dq:1,always:1,st:-.25,nc:1,heat:16,ok:"The ref throws it out. Nobody wins, and neither is happy about it.",g:"The ref calls for the bell, and both villains turn on the ref — then each other — then the ref again. The crowd chants \"We want more!\""},
 {t:"{B} lies down and lets {A} pin them",always:1,st:-.25,heat:6,ok:"{B} grins, lies flat, and {A} poses with a single finger on the chest. One, two, three. The crowd is disgusted. They've been robbed of a match.",g:"{B} looks at {A}, smiles, and lies down. {A} rests one finger on the chest. Three. Garbage rains into the ring as they celebrate together. Commentary calls it a disgrace."}]},
{id:'top',w:2,ntrait:'monster|suplex',text:"{A} climbs to the top rope while {B} lies flat in the middle of the ring.",ch:[
 {t:"Go for the highest-risk move in their arsenal",iAn:.5,s:"ring",d:.2,st:.75,fat:6,ok:"They nail it! The crowd can't believe it.",g:"{A} launches, twists in mid-air, and lands it flush. A beat of silence while the crowd processes what they saw — then a roar. That's going to be on every highlight reel.",no:"{A} overshoots and crashes.",b:"{A} jumps, under-rotates, and lands knees-first on {B}'s chest. The ref looks worried and the crowd goes quiet."},
 {t:"Play it safe and climb back down",always:1,st:0,ok:"The crowd groans, but {A} wins anyway.",g:"{A} climbs down, gives a little shrug to the crowd, and wins with a simple move. Smart. Boring, but smart."},
 {t:"Point to the fans, then fly",al:"f",s:"pop",d:.15,st:.75,popA:2,fat:6,ok:"{A} points to the crowd, they roar, and {A} flies. A picture-perfect highlight.",g:"{A} points to a sign in the crowd, holds it for a beat, and flies. Perfect splash. The fans chant {A}'s name until the bell.",no:"{B} rolls away at the last second.",b:"{A} points to the fans, wobbles, and has to jump off early to avoid falling. It just looks like a fall anyway."},
 {t:"Taunt the crowd from the top rope",al:"h",s:"mic",d:.1,st:.25,popA:1,ok:"The boos peak just as {A} comes crashing down on {B}.",g:"{A} taunts so long the boos shake the ring, then lands a perfect elbow from the top. Pure villainy, perfectly timed.",no:"{B} gets up and crotches {A} on the top rope.",b:"{A} taunts so long that {B} gets up, walks over and pulls them down."}]}];
